- [Tom] Yeah, please, thank you.

250
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:43,600
(quirky music)

251
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:46,967
- Whoa, whoa, it smells
like a monkey house in here.

252
00:09:46,967 --> 00:09:48,200
- Hello again.

253
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:50,400
- [Tom] Got a long
mic cord there.

254
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:53,100
- Boys and girls, it's just
weeks before Christmas,

255
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:55,267
and Santa and his helpers
are working overtime

256
00:09:55,267 --> 00:09:57,033
to make sure that
there's enough toys

257
00:09:57,033 --> 00:09:59,733
for the kids all over the world.

258
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:00,933
- [Joel] All over the world!

259
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:02,700
- Santa's a pretty
busy man, but I'm sure

260
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:05,867
he'd like to say a
few words to you kids.

261
00:10:05,867 --> 00:10:07,733
- [Tom] Oh, I dunno.

262
00:10:07,733 --> 00:10:08,900
- Hello, Santa.

263
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:11,000
- Get the hell out of my shop!

264
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,400
- Oh, oh, hello, boys and girls!

265
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:17,700
- Smoking is good
for you, ho ho ho!

266
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:20,033
- Andy, you caught me
at a very busy time.

267
00:10:20,033 --> 00:10:22,700
- Well, you think you'll
be ready by Christmas Eve?

268
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:25,200
- Well, we've never
disappointed the kids yet.

269
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:27,733
- [Joel] Except
for the poor ones.

270
00:10:27,733 --> 00:10:29,300
- Tell me, is it
true that this year,

271
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:32,333
there's a rumor that you're
going to use a rocket sled?

272
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:36,633
- No sirree, we're going out
the good old-fashioned way.

273
00:10:36,633 --> 00:10:38,433
- [Joel] Guns a-blazing.

274
00:10:38,433 --> 00:10:41,867
- Prancer and Dancer
and Donder and Blitzen

275
00:10:41,867 --> 00:10:44,333
and Vixen and Nixon.

276
00:10:44,333 --> 00:10:46,500
- [Tom] Yes, and what's
in the pipe, sir?

277
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:49,900
- Oh, I always, consarn it,
I get those names mixed up,

278
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,667
but the kids know their names.

279
00:10:51,667 --> 00:10:52,733
- Yeah, 'cause they're sober.

280
00:10:52,733 --> 00:10:54,367
- Santa, there you are.

281
00:10:54,367 --> 00:10:55,867
- [Joel] It's Barbara Bush!
- We have so much to do,

282
00:10:55,867 --> 00:10:58,967
and you stand here dawdling,
talking to this visitor.

283
00:10:58,967 --> 00:11:02,233
- Mr. Anderson,
this is Mrs. Claus.

284
00:11:02,233 --> 00:11:03,167
- [Tom] Hands off.

285
00:11:03,167 --> 00:11:05,133
- Dear, we're on television.

286
00:11:05,133 --> 00:11:06,967
- How do you do, Mr. Anderson?
- Ma'am.

287
00:11:06,967 --> 00:11:08,200
- Now, I want you
to go and finish

288
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,733
painting those hobby horses!

289
00:11:10,733 --> 00:11:11,700
Television?

290
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:13,600
Did you say we're on television?

291
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:15,700
♪ Ed Sullivan ♪

292
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:17,700
- Why didn't you tell me?

293
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:19,100
My hair's a mess!

294
00:11:20,333 --> 00:11:21,733
- [Joel] Hi, Mom.

295
00:11:22,933 --> 00:11:24,100
- [Tom] When she thinks
of the mass media,

296
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,467
she touches herself.

297
00:11:25,467 --> 00:11:27,267
(laughing)

298
00:11:27,267 --> 00:11:29,000
- (laughing) We're
having her committed.

299
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,500
- Come along, Mr. Anderson.

300
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:35,467
And I'll show you some of the
new toys we're turning out.

301
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:37,600
- Oh, looks like C.
Everett Koop's children

302
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,867
are employed here.

303
00:11:38,867 --> 00:11:41,233
- [Tom] Union meeting
tonight, pass it on.

304
00:11:41,233 --> 00:11:43,267
- Everything is a-okay, Santa.

305
00:11:43,267 --> 00:11:44,100
- Good man.

306
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:45,367
- [Joel] Blinky, sir.

307
00:11:45,367 --> 00:11:46,600
- Winky is in charge
of our special parts.

308
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,167
- [Joel] Blinky.

309
00:11:48,167 --> 00:11:52,767
- Oh, uh, now here, here
is the latest toy rocket.

310
00:11:52,767 --> 00:11:55,500
It runs on real rocket fuel.

311
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:56,667
- Really?

312
00:11:56,667 --> 00:11:58,200
I've been wondering,
what is this

313
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,800
strange little
creature over there?

314
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,000
- I'm Batman.

315
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,600
- Oh, Winky made that.

316
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,533
- [Joel] Blinky, sir.

317
00:12:03,533 --> 00:12:05,367
- That's his idea of a Martian.

318
00:12:05,367 --> 00:12:06,867
- A Martian?

319
00:12:06,867 --> 00:12:08,433
Wowwee wow, I'd hate to
meet a creature like that

320
00:12:08,433 --> 00:12:09,700
on a dark night.

321
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,300
- [Tom] I'd hate to meet
Blinky on a dark night.

322
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:13,100
- I wonder if there
really are people on Mars.

323
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,100
- Well, who knows.
- Makes ya think,

324
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:15,600
don't it, huh?

325
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,800
- Well, if there are, I hope
they have someone like you

326
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:18,967
up there, Santa, to
bring joy and good cheer

327
00:12:18,967 --> 00:12:20,600
to all the Martian children.

328
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:24,167
- [Tom] Ho ho ho,
you flatter me.

329
00:12:24,167 --> 00:12:27,467
- Keep going, Winky,
Christmas Eve is coming soon.

330
00:12:27,467 --> 00:12:29,867
Now, Mr. Anderson, I
wanna show you some--

331
00:12:29,867 --> 00:12:32,667
(whooshing)
(imitating whooshing)

332
00:12:32,667 --> 00:12:35,033
- [Tom] Meanwhile, at
Oscar Wilde's house.

333
00:12:35,033 --> 00:12:37,300
- Dropo, you lazy
good-for-nothing, where are you!

334
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:39,033
- [Crow] Tonight
I'm a space pirate.

335
00:12:39,033 --> 00:12:40,333
Permission to come aboard!

336
00:12:40,333 --> 00:12:41,633
- [Tom] Woohoo.

337
00:12:41,633 --> 00:12:42,467
- Dropo.

338
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:45,233
Dropo, wake up!

339
00:12:45,233 --> 00:12:46,067
Wake up!

340
00:12:48,533 --> 00:12:50,767
(chuckling)

341
00:12:50,767 --> 00:12:52,767
- [Joel] Ah, ah, ah,
get the spiders off!

342
00:12:52,767 --> 00:12:54,367
Off, off me!

343
00:12:54,367 --> 00:12:56,100
- Turn off that tickle ray!

344
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:59,667
- [Tom] Before I can't fake
laugh any more! (laughing)

345
00:12:59,667 --> 00:13:00,600
- Stand up.

346
00:13:02,233 --> 00:13:03,733
- [Tom] Hey.

347
00:13:03,733 --> 00:13:04,967
- [Kimar] Stand up!

348
00:13:04,967 --> 00:13:06,067
Stand up!

349
00:13:06,067 --> 00:13:07,633
- [Tom] And be counted!

350
00:13:07,633 --> 00:13:09,400
- I'm sorry, Chief Kimar, sir.

351
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:12,133
- Dropo, you are the
laziest man on Mars.

352
00:13:12,133 --> 00:13:14,267
Why are you sleeping
during the working hours?

353
00:13:14,267 --> 00:13:15,333
- [Tom] 'Cause I'm the
laziest man on Mars.

354
00:13:15,333 --> 00:13:17,000
- I wasn't sleeping, Chief.

355
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,667
It's just that I haven't
been able to sleep

356
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:20,233
these last few nights.

357
00:13:20,233 --> 00:13:22,733
- He's been drunk
off his Martian butt.

358
00:13:22,733 --> 00:13:24,233
- So I was just practicing.

359
00:13:24,233 --> 00:13:25,700
(laughing)

360
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:27,167
- [Tom] (chuckling) Kill him.

361
00:13:27,167 --> 00:13:30,400
- Well, I suggest you
practice doing your work.

362
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:31,433
Where's Lady Momar?

363
00:13:31,433 --> 00:13:32,667
- [Joel] Qaddafi?

364
00:13:32,667 --> 00:13:33,600
- She went to the
food pill center

365
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,600
to get some new food pills.

366
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,533
- See, 'cause it's Mars.

367
00:13:36,533 --> 00:13:37,367
Yeah.

368
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,667
- It's no wonder.

369
00:13:39,667 --> 00:13:41,133
They sit in front of
the video set all day

370
00:13:41,133 --> 00:13:43,667
watching those ridiculous
Earth programs.

371
00:13:43,667 --> 00:13:44,867
It confuses them.

372
00:13:44,867 --> 00:13:46,033
- [Tom] Especially "Twin Peaks."

373
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:47,233
- Where are they?

374
00:13:47,233 --> 00:13:50,467
- Oh, in there,
watching Earth programs.

375
00:13:50,467 --> 00:13:52,967
- [Joel] Uh, it's Sweeps Week.

376
00:13:54,733 --> 00:13:57,533
- [Tom] Open, Coco
the Clown room!

377
00:13:59,367 --> 00:14:00,867
- [Andy] Say, Santa,
what have we here?

378
00:14:00,867 --> 00:14:02,400
- [Joel] You know, Pia
Zadora never got much taller

379
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,233
than she is in this.

380
00:14:04,233 --> 00:14:08,467
- [Santa] Walks, talks,
cries, and she even sings.

381
00:14:08,467 --> 00:14:09,733
- But she wants to direct.

382
00:14:09,733 --> 00:14:11,967
- [Andy] Almost like a
real live little girl.

383
00:14:11,967 --> 00:14:14,767
- [Santa] That she
is, sir, that she is.

384
00:14:14,767 --> 00:14:17,700
All she needs is
tender loving care.

385
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,033
- [Tom] And 20 bucks worth

386
00:14:19,033 --> 00:14:21,067
of batteries.
- Bromar, what is a doll?

387
00:14:21,067 --> 00:14:22,800
- I don't know, Girmar.

388
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:24,900
What is tender loving care?

389
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:26,233
- I don't know either.

390
00:14:26,233 --> 00:14:27,567
- Bomar, Girmar.

391
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,933
I've told you not to watch
those silly Earth programs.

392
00:14:31,933 --> 00:14:34,533
- Like "Firing Line."
- Now, go to sleep.

393
00:14:34,533 --> 00:14:36,400
- Must we go to
sleep now, Father?

394
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:38,700
I want to see Santa
Claus some more.

395
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:40,467
- I want to see more toys.

396
00:14:40,467 --> 00:14:42,167
- No, go to sleep.

397
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:44,333
- Will you buy me a
Golden Globe, then?

398
00:14:44,333 --> 00:14:45,833
- [Tom] Why, sure.

399
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,567
Well, she'll serve 12, and with
a little Martian seasoning,

400
00:14:52,567 --> 00:14:54,567
she'll make a
tempting main course.

401
00:14:54,567 --> 00:14:57,233
(smacking lips)

402
00:14:58,867 --> 00:15:01,433
(mellow music)

403
00:15:03,733 --> 00:15:06,367
- We need your advice, Chochem.

404
00:15:06,367 --> 00:15:07,600
- [Joel] Buy Polaroid?

405
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:09,600
- Something is wrong
with our children.

406
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:10,600
- [Tom] On Saturn 3.

407
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:12,500
- They eat not, they sleep not.

408
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:13,733
- They are not.

409
00:15:13,733 --> 00:15:15,200
- Their only interest
is watching meaningless

410
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:17,367
Earth programs on the video.

411
00:15:17,367 --> 00:15:19,167
- [Joel] Are there
any other kind?

412
00:15:19,167 --> 00:15:20,100
But I digress.

413
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,400
- What time of year is it now?

414
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,200
- [Kimar] It is the
middle of Septober.

415
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,733
- [Tom] Oh, time
for Septoberfest.

416
00:15:25,733 --> 00:15:26,933
- No, no.

417
00:15:26,933 --> 00:15:27,767
Not here.

418
00:15:29,033 --> 00:15:30,933
I mean on Earth.

419
00:15:30,933 --> 00:15:32,767
- [Joel] Guy looks
like a troll doll.

420
00:15:32,767 --> 00:15:33,933
- [Tom] He does.

421
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:35,767
- Ah yes.
- I had Jell-o today.

422
00:15:35,767 --> 00:15:38,433
- It is early December on Earth.

423
00:15:40,867 --> 00:15:43,800
Close to the time
of the Christmas.

424
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:46,467
- [Tom] Uh, hello,
Mars to Chochem.

425
00:15:46,467 --> 00:15:48,633
- That explains it.

426
00:15:48,633 --> 00:15:50,333
- What is a Christmas?

427
00:15:50,333 --> 00:15:53,667
- [Joel] It's a Christian
holiday ruined by commercialism.

428
00:15:53,667 --> 00:15:57,433
- Of great joy and peace
on the planet Earth.

429
00:15:58,867 --> 00:16:01,033
- [Tom] Look, we caught you at
a bad time, we'll come back.

430
00:16:01,033 --> 00:16:05,700
- And to children, it is
also a time of anticipation.

431
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:08,333
- Hey, uh, just in case,
where are your nitro pills?

432
00:16:08,333 --> 00:16:11,333
- As they await the
arrival of Santa Claus.

433
00:16:11,333 --> 00:16:12,800
- [Joel] He's Howard Hughes!

434
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:14,033
- [Tom] Oh!

435
00:16:14,033 --> 00:16:15,000
- And his gifts.
- Bah!

436
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:15,933
(all bleating)

437
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:17,467
Nonsense.

438
00:16:17,467 --> 00:16:19,967
- What has this to do with
our children, ancient one?

439
00:16:19,967 --> 00:16:22,533
- We have no children on Mars.

440
00:16:22,533 --> 00:16:24,133
- I have no son.

441
00:16:24,133 --> 00:16:28,467
- They have children's
bodies, but with adult minds.

442
00:16:28,467 --> 00:16:30,433
- [Tom] Oh, like Drew Barrymore.

443
00:16:30,433 --> 00:16:33,033
- They do not have a childhood.

444
00:16:35,567 --> 00:16:38,667
I've seen this
coming for centuries.

445
00:16:38,667 --> 00:16:40,100
- Why didn't you tell us, Pops?

446
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:43,867
- They are born, our
electronic teaching machines

447
00:16:43,867 --> 00:16:46,267
are attached to their brains
(yawning)

448
00:16:46,267 --> 00:16:49,433
while they are in their cradles.

449
00:16:49,433 --> 00:16:53,400
Information is fed into their
minds in a constant stream.

450
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:54,867
(whistling)

451
00:16:54,867 --> 00:16:55,967
- Look, you're breaking
my heart, Gramps.

452
00:16:55,967 --> 00:16:58,000
Can you get on with it?

453
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,767
- They are adults.

454
00:16:59,767 --> 00:17:02,267
- [Tom] And they go
through shoes like crazy.

455
00:17:02,267 --> 00:17:04,600
- They never played.

456
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:07,300
They never learned to have fun.

457
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:08,867
- Oh, he's fading fast.

458
00:17:08,867 --> 00:17:09,700
- And now.

459
00:17:11,233 --> 00:17:13,167
Now they are rebelling.

460
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,333
- What do you advise?

461
00:17:16,333 --> 00:17:21,333
- The children must be
allowed to be children again.

462
00:17:22,067 --> 00:17:23,400
They must learn to play.

463
00:17:24,567 --> 00:17:27,900
They must learn what
it means to have fun.

464
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:30,200
- [Joel] Everything I know
I learned in kindergarten.

465
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:33,600
- We need a Santa Claus on Mars.

466
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:35,700
- Yeah, and you need
a sedative, old man.

467
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:37,500
(thunder rumbling)

468
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:42,333
- [Tom] Diarrhea is like
a storm raging inside you.

469
00:17:42,333 --> 00:17:45,133
- Look, uh, you're a busy
man, we'll come back.

470
00:17:45,133 --> 00:17:46,233
Ooh!

471
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:48,067
- [Joel] Next show at 10:30.

472
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:49,533
- [Tom] Hey, let's give
it up for the old man.

473
00:17:49,533 --> 00:17:51,433
How about it!
(cheering)

474
00:17:51,433 --> 00:17:53,767
Well, scratch the Chochem idea.

475
00:17:53,767 --> 00:17:55,867
So, you catch any of that?

476
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:57,367
- Santa Claus on Mars?

477
00:17:57,367 --> 00:17:58,967
- [Joel] I think it would
go something like this.

478
00:17:58,967 --> 00:18:00,500
- Santa Claus.

479
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:02,100
There's only one Santa
Claus, and he's on Earth.

480
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:03,400
(laughing)

481
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,667
- Sorry.

482
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:06,867
- Well, I guess that
takes care of that.

483
00:18:06,867 --> 00:18:08,900
Didn't I tell you it
was a foolish idea

484
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:10,633
to seek advice
from that old man?

485
00:18:10,633 --> 00:18:12,000
- This is a serious
matter, Voldar,

486
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,733
and desperate problems
require desperate deeds.

487
00:18:14,733 --> 00:18:15,933
- [Joel] Done dirt cheap.

488
00:18:15,933 --> 00:18:17,867
- Earth has had Santa
Claus long enough.

489
00:18:17,867 --> 00:18:19,333
We will bring him to Mars.

490
00:18:19,333 --> 00:18:20,533
- I'm against it!

491
00:18:20,533 --> 00:18:22,533
Our children are fine
the way they are.

492
00:18:22,533 --> 00:18:25,333
I don't want any Santa Claus
bringing them toys and games.

493
00:18:25,333 --> 00:18:28,000
They'll start playing and
laughing and running underfoot.

494
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,000
They'll become a nuisance.

495
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,700
- I've made my decision.

496
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:31,833
We leave for Earth tonight.

497
00:18:31,833 --> 00:18:33,467
- Pack your other mustache.

498
00:18:33,467 --> 00:18:34,600
- Rigna, Lomas.

499
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,867
- [Tom] Rico,
Youngblood, Dipstick.

500
00:18:36,867 --> 00:18:39,867
(suspenseful music)

501
00:18:42,733 --> 00:18:44,233
Uh-huh.

502
00:18:44,233 --> 00:18:48,867
Okay, thank you, you can lose
this shot now, scene's over.

503
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:51,167
- [Crow] This is better.

504
00:18:51,167 --> 00:18:52,467
- [Joel] Cricket lighter away!

505
00:18:52,467 --> 00:18:54,300
Cricket lighter.

506
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:56,933
- [Tom] You know, if they
cancel "Battlestar Galactica",

507
00:18:56,933 --> 00:18:58,767
I'm gonna kill myself.

508
00:19:04,567 --> 00:19:06,500
- Hey, look, their ship
runs on a Simon game.

509
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:07,900
(Tom beeping)

510
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:09,033
- [Joel] Stratego!

511
00:19:09,033 --> 00:19:11,633
- [Tom] You sunk my battleship!

512
00:19:14,100 --> 00:19:15,467
- Gentlemen, we can't all be

513
00:19:15,467 --> 00:19:18,133
the Honey Nut Cheerios honeybee.

514
00:19:21,067 --> 00:19:23,267
- Approaching
projected Earth orbit.

515
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:26,333
- [Joel] I know, I'm the
one that steered us into it.

516
00:19:26,333 --> 00:19:29,767
- Fire portside rockets
number one and number two.

517
00:19:29,767 --> 00:19:33,700
- Portside rockets number
one and number two, fired.

518
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:34,767
(hissing)

519
00:19:34,767 --> 00:19:37,000
- [Tom] Whoa, lentils, phew.

520
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,400
- Entering Earth orbit.

521
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:41,933
All right, Voldar, now
to find Santa Claus.

522
00:19:41,933 --> 00:19:43,100
- All right.

523
00:19:43,100 --> 00:19:44,533
- Turn the magnascope
to third power.

524
00:19:44,533 --> 00:19:47,633
(electronic beeping)

525
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,100
We're over a city of some kind.

526
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:52,400
- [Joel] The Big Apple.

527
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,967
- [Tom] Des Moines?

528
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:58,600
- So that's what the Earth
people call a city, eh?

529
00:19:58,600 --> 00:19:59,900
How primitive.

530
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:01,767
- [Tom] Oh, everything's
better on Mars.

531
00:20:01,767 --> 00:20:03,633
- Look at all those
buildings above ground.

532
00:20:03,633 --> 00:20:05,067
Why, we could destroy that city

533
00:20:05,067 --> 00:20:07,233
with one blast of our Q ray.

534
00:20:07,233 --> 00:20:09,700
- We did not come here
to destroy anyone.

535
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:12,133
Our only purpose is to bring
Santa Claus back to Mars.

536
00:20:12,133 --> 00:20:14,900
- And maybe stop for an
egg cream, but that's it.

537
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:18,333
- Let's see if we can
locate Santa Claus.

538
00:20:19,733 --> 00:20:21,400
He wears a red suit.

539
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,867
- Mm-hm.

540
00:20:22,867 --> 00:20:24,667
- Trimmed with white fur, and
he has a long white beard.

541
00:20:24,667 --> 00:20:27,167
- Wait a minute, you just
described Huggy Bear.

542
00:20:27,167 --> 00:20:28,967
- It's like looking for
a speck of space dust

543
00:20:28,967 --> 00:20:30,367
in a comet's tail.

544
00:20:30,367 --> 00:20:31,900
- [Tom] Ooh, good analogy.

545
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:33,600
- Wait a minute, I see him!

546
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:34,800
I see Santa Claus!

547
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,033
- [Joel] And he's kissing Mommy!

548
00:20:36,033 --> 00:20:38,467
(Tom gasping)

549
00:20:38,467 --> 00:20:39,767
- I see him too!

550
00:20:39,767 --> 00:20:41,233
- He's standing on the
corner ringing a bell.

551
00:20:41,233 --> 00:20:43,333
- No he's not, he's
standing near the entrance

552
00:20:43,333 --> 00:20:46,533
of a large building, next
to a large black kettle.

553
00:20:46,533 --> 00:20:48,533
- He's standing on the
corner, Kimar, he's...

554
00:20:48,533 --> 00:20:49,533
Wait a minute!

555
00:20:49,533 --> 00:20:51,067
I see another one!

556
00:20:51,067 --> 00:20:52,567
- Why, there are hundreds
of Santa Clauses down there!

557
00:20:52,567 --> 00:20:54,867
- Santa is within all of us.

558
00:20:54,867 --> 00:20:56,167
- Just one.

559
00:20:56,167 --> 00:20:59,067
And with so many,
they won't miss one.

560
00:20:59,067 --> 00:21:01,067
Prepare for landing
on next orbit.

561
00:21:01,067 --> 00:21:02,967
- We interrupt our program
with a special bulletin.

562
00:21:02,967 --> 00:21:04,133
- [Tom] I'm Dick York.

563
00:21:04,133 --> 00:21:05,300
- An unidentified
object has been spotted

564
00:21:05,300 --> 00:21:06,933
in orbit around the Earth.

565
00:21:06,933 --> 00:21:08,533
The Soviet Union
denies it has launched

566
00:21:08,533 --> 00:21:10,167
any new space satellites.

567
00:21:10,167 --> 00:21:11,500
- Like they could afford to.

568
00:21:11,500 --> 00:21:12,767
- Our radar stations are
tracking the spaceship,

569
00:21:12,767 --> 00:21:14,433
or whatever it is.

570
00:21:14,433 --> 00:21:16,600
The U.S. Air Force has
alerted all defense commands

571
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:18,367
and retaliatory units.

572
00:21:18,367 --> 00:21:19,567
- [Joel] You know, I
didn't know the military

573
00:21:19,567 --> 00:21:20,933
had a study hall.

574
00:21:20,933 --> 00:21:24,033
(militaristic music)

575
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:27,833
- [Tom] Roger, paper
towel rolls are

576
00:21:27,833 --> 00:21:29,900
on the patio table, over.

577
00:21:34,867 --> 00:21:37,867
- But first, a tour
of Paisley Park.

578
00:21:40,033 --> 00:21:44,133
- [Joel] Dear Hair Club for
Men, I need help big time.

579
00:21:44,133 --> 00:21:45,667
Would you consider?

580
00:21:47,133 --> 00:21:51,433
- [Tom] And then a large-scale
bowling pin is put into use.

581
00:21:51,433 --> 00:21:52,267
Morning.

582
00:21:52,267 --> 00:21:53,100
- [Joel] Good morning.

583
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:54,800
- [Tom] Good morning.

584
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:57,833
(sighing) Oh boy.

585
00:21:57,833 --> 00:21:59,933
- Wow, there's a ton of
stock footage out there!

586
00:21:59,933 --> 00:22:02,267
- Sir, Earth radar beams
are bouncing off our ship.

587
00:22:02,267 --> 00:22:05,000
- Well, it certainly
took them long enough.

588
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:08,067
Voldar, turn on
the radar shield.

589
00:22:08,067 --> 00:22:10,033
- Misfunctioning
of radar shield.

590
00:22:10,033 --> 00:22:12,667
- Rigna, check the radar box.

591
00:22:12,667 --> 00:22:14,800
- [Joel] Not the toy
box, the radar box!

592
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:16,733
- Radar shield functioning.

593
00:22:16,733 --> 00:22:18,533
What was wrong, Rigna?

594
00:22:18,533 --> 00:22:19,967
- A slight case of Dropo.

595
00:22:19,967 --> 00:22:22,300
- [All] Womp-womp-womp-womp!

596
00:22:23,767 --> 00:22:25,833
- I went to the launghing pad
so I could say goodbye to you,

597
00:22:25,833 --> 00:22:27,333
and I remembered!

598
00:22:27,333 --> 00:22:29,700
I've never been to Earth, so
I thought I wanted to see it.

599
00:22:29,700 --> 00:22:31,400
- I may leave you there
in place of Santa Claus.

600
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:33,533
Now get below, I'll
deal with you later.

601
00:22:33,533 --> 00:22:35,133
- Sorry, Mr. Martian Captain.

602
00:22:35,133 --> 00:22:36,833
Oh, what the hell, the controls!

603
00:22:36,833 --> 00:22:39,367
- [Tom] What, did Sherwood
Schwartz write this?

604
00:22:39,367 --> 00:22:41,533
- [Joel] That's our Dropo.

605
00:22:41,533 --> 00:22:43,300
He'll be back, ha ha!

606
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,567
- Prepare to land.

607
00:22:46,567 --> 00:22:49,033
We'll set down in that
field near the lake.

608
00:22:49,033 --> 00:22:50,267
- [Tom] Neat.

609
00:22:50,267 --> 00:22:52,067
- Rocket silencer set.

610
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:56,033
- Rotor rockets number
one and two, fire.

611
00:22:56,033 --> 00:22:57,033
(whirring)

612
00:22:57,033 --> 00:22:58,000
- Whoa.
- Lentils.

613
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,500
- [Tom] Ooh.

614
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:01,667
- All this trouble over a
fat little man in a red suit.

615
00:23:01,667 --> 00:23:03,500
- [Tom] Truman Capote?

616
00:23:04,467 --> 00:23:06,233
- Here's another UFO bulletin.

617
00:23:06,233 --> 00:23:07,400
- [Joel] I'm high.

618
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:08,533
- The defense department
has just announced

619
00:23:08,533 --> 00:23:10,167
that the unidentified
flying object

620
00:23:10,167 --> 00:23:12,633
has suddenly disappeared
from our radar screens.

621
00:23:12,633 --> 00:23:13,900
- So to hell with it.

622
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:15,900
- [Tom] Speaking of
disappearing, guys.

623
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:18,233
- It may be a spaceship
from some other planet

624
00:23:18,233 --> 00:23:21,633
which has the ability to
nullify our radar beams.

625
00:23:21,633 --> 00:23:23,867
Because of the
ominous situation, the
president has ordered

626
00:23:23,867 --> 00:23:27,033
the strategic air
command into action.

627
00:23:34,667 --> 00:23:36,933
- You know, I think
it's kind of, uh,

628
00:23:36,933 --> 00:23:38,967
hot to be wearing
these scarves in here.

629
00:23:38,967 --> 00:23:40,133
- Oh, well the
scarves are a must.

630
00:23:40,133 --> 00:23:41,333
You can't go caroling
without a scarf.

631
00:23:41,333 --> 00:23:42,833
You'll catch your death.

632
00:23:42,833 --> 00:23:44,400
- Yeah, and you were like
one of those kids I remember

633
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:47,533
in high school that used
to sell the most candy bars

634
00:23:47,533 --> 00:23:48,967
for the marching band.

635
00:23:48,967 --> 00:23:51,100
- President of the
swing choir, too.

636
00:23:51,100 --> 00:23:52,267
- Definitely.

637
00:23:52,267 --> 00:23:53,700
- Thanks, Joel Robinson,
thanks, Tom Servo.

638
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:55,267
- What a kiss-up, this guy.

639
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:56,667
- Okay now, if you'll all
look at your sheet music,

640
00:23:56,667 --> 00:23:58,333
we can rehearse my new song.

641
00:23:58,333 --> 00:23:59,900
- You wrote a Christmas song?

642
00:23:59,900 --> 00:24:01,800
- Hey, there's no tradition
like a new tradition.

643
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:04,267
- Wait a minute, "Let's Have
a Patrick Swayze Christmas?"

644
00:24:04,267 --> 00:24:06,633
- Yeah, yeah, based on my
favorite movie, "Road House."

645
00:24:06,633 --> 00:24:07,900
- Come on, what the
heck does Patrick Swayze

646
00:24:07,900 --> 00:24:09,067
have to do with Christmas?

647
00:24:09,067 --> 00:24:10,333
- Hey, you keep
Christmas in your way

648
00:24:10,333 --> 00:24:11,667
and let me keep
it in mine, okay?

649
00:24:11,667 --> 00:24:13,133
- Oh, geez.

650
00:24:13,133 --> 00:24:14,733
- Come on, Servo, it seems
like a nice enough sentiment.

651
00:24:14,733 --> 00:24:16,333
We can give it a shot, come on.

652
00:24:16,333 --> 00:24:17,567
- All right, okay, okay.

653
00:24:17,567 --> 00:24:19,833
Uh, 12/8 time, key
of A flat major.

654
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:21,700
Cambot, shoot 'em the tune.

655
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:24,200
Okay, you'll just have to
stay with me, everybody, okay?

656
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:25,767
Your parts are written out.

657
00:24:25,767 --> 00:24:29,000
"Let's Have a Patrick Swayze
Christmas" by Crow T. Robot.

658
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:30,433
(clearing throat)

659
00:24:30,433 --> 00:24:33,567
- Paul, let's have a
Patrick Swayze Christmas.

660
00:24:33,567 --> 00:24:34,933
- Right, hit it, Cambot.

661
00:24:34,933 --> 00:24:36,900
(mellow music)

662
00:24:36,900 --> 00:24:38,400
- Oh, oh, I start, I get it.

663
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:39,800
Okay, pick it up.

664
00:24:41,267 --> 00:24:46,233
♪ Open up your heart and let the
Patrick Swayze Christmas in ♪

665
00:24:48,100 --> 00:24:53,100
♪ We'll gather at the road
house with our next of kin ♪

666
00:24:54,267 --> 00:24:55,733
- Not bad.

667
00:24:55,733 --> 00:25:00,167
♪ And Santa can be our
regular Saturday night thing ♪

668
00:25:01,700 --> 00:25:06,633
♪ We'll decorate a bar stool
and gather 'round and sing ♪

669
00:25:08,233 --> 00:25:13,233
♪ Oh let's have a Patrick
Swayze Christmas this year ♪

670
00:25:15,733 --> 00:25:20,733
♪ Or we'll tear your throat
out and kick you in the ear ♪

671
00:25:21,867 --> 00:25:23,800
- Hold it, hold it,
Cambot, stop it.

672
00:25:23,800 --> 00:25:26,300
Crow, I don't know
if I think this is

673
00:25:26,300 --> 00:25:28,733
an appropriate sentiment
any more for Christmas.

674
00:25:28,733 --> 00:25:29,933
- Hey, what, like a
good action sequence

675
00:25:29,933 --> 00:25:31,333
don't belong at Christmas?

676
00:25:31,333 --> 00:25:34,033
- Well, no, it's just
that I've never heard of

677
00:25:34,033 --> 00:25:36,633
an action sequence in a
Christmas carol before.

678
00:25:36,633 --> 00:25:38,100
- Well then, grab
hold of your socks

679
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:39,833
and read on, Joel Robinson!

680
00:25:39,833 --> 00:25:42,033
- Okay, pick it up from
measure 20, Cambot.

681
00:25:42,033 --> 00:25:43,633
(mellow music)

682
00:25:43,633 --> 00:25:44,800
Lovely intro though,
very tasteful.

683
00:25:44,800 --> 00:25:46,967
- Thank you.
- I like that.

684
00:25:48,467 --> 00:25:53,267
♪ It's my way or the highway
this Christmas at my bar ♪

685
00:25:55,167 --> 00:25:57,967
♪ I'll have to smash
your kneecaps ♪

686
00:25:57,967 --> 00:26:02,067
♪ If you bastards touch my car ♪

687
00:26:02,067 --> 00:26:07,067
♪ I got the word that Santa has
been stealing from the till ♪

688
00:26:08,867 --> 00:26:12,533
♪ I think that that
right jolly old elf ♪

689
00:26:12,533 --> 00:26:15,333
♪ Better make out his will ♪

690
00:26:15,333 --> 00:26:20,333
♪ Oh let's have a Patrick
Swayze Christmas one and all ♪

691
00:26:22,767 --> 00:26:26,167
♪ And this can be the haziest ♪

692
00:26:26,167 --> 00:26:27,667
(lively piano solo)

693
00:26:27,667 --> 00:26:28,733
- Whoa.
- Ooh.

694
00:26:29,900 --> 00:26:33,433
♪ This can be the laziest ♪

695
00:26:33,433 --> 00:26:36,733
(lively piano solo)

696
00:26:36,733 --> 00:26:41,733
♪ This can be the Swayziest
Christmas of them all ♪

697
00:26:47,967 --> 00:26:51,467
♪ La la la la la la ah-ha ♪

698
00:26:52,667 --> 00:26:54,067
- How long before it
becomes a standard?

699
00:26:54,067 --> 00:26:55,267
- I think you gotta
come with me, come on.

700
00:26:55,267 --> 00:26:56,633
(shouting)

701
00:26:56,633 --> 00:26:58,267
- We'll be right back.

702
00:26:58,267 --> 00:27:00,533
Save a leg for me.

703
00:27:00,533 --> 00:27:03,067
(mellow music)

704
00:27:06,133 --> 00:27:08,667
- Fire retro rockets
number five and six.

705
00:27:08,667 --> 00:27:09,867
- I got a million of 'em.

706
00:27:09,867 --> 00:27:12,367
- Retro rockets
five and six, fired.

707
00:27:12,367 --> 00:27:13,367
(whirring)

708
00:27:13,367 --> 00:27:14,767
- Yep, lentils.
- Lentils.

709
00:27:14,767 --> 00:27:16,400
- Pretty much.
- Yeah.

710
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:18,300
- [Joel] Uh, polka dots
and moonbeams, sir.

711
00:27:18,300 --> 00:27:20,467
(beeping)

712
00:27:21,567 --> 00:27:23,333
- Get that, would ya?

713
00:27:25,833 --> 00:27:27,867
- Lower landing legs.

714
00:27:27,867 --> 00:27:30,633
- I've got the landing legs.

715
00:27:30,633 --> 00:27:34,633
- [Joel] Real sophisticated
space leg controls, I like that.

716
00:27:34,633 --> 00:27:36,800
- [Tom] He loves his work.

717
00:27:40,433 --> 00:27:42,100
- [Joel] Gosh, he's
good at that thing.

718
00:27:42,100 --> 00:27:42,933
- [Tom] Yep.

719
00:27:42,933 --> 00:27:44,200
- Landing legs lowered.

720
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:45,933
- Attention, crew,
this is Kimar.

721
00:27:45,933 --> 00:27:47,500
- Today's blue
light special is--

722
00:27:47,500 --> 00:27:50,267
- Rigna, Voldar and I will
leave the ship to investigate.

723
00:27:50,267 --> 00:27:52,200
- [Joel] Stinky,
Softbatch, Clamdip.

724
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:54,200
- And Dropo will stay on
board on constant alert

725
00:27:54,200 --> 00:27:56,200
for immediate blast-off.

726
00:27:57,633 --> 00:27:58,767
- [Tom] There.

727
00:27:58,767 --> 00:28:00,233
(dramatic music)

728
00:28:00,233 --> 00:28:01,933
(imitating engine noises)

729
00:28:01,933 --> 00:28:04,367
- [Tom] Ooh, getting roasted.

730
00:28:05,733 --> 00:28:07,200
- [Announcer] The Defense
Department believes

731
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:08,633
that the object spotted on--

732
00:28:08,633 --> 00:28:10,367
- Ah, Splendor in the Leaves.

733
00:28:10,367 --> 00:28:11,833
- [Tom] Mm-hm.

734
00:28:11,833 --> 00:28:12,767
- [Announcer] Nothing more
than a meteor which burned up

735
00:28:12,767 --> 00:28:14,800
when it entered our atmosphere.

736
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:18,300
Professor Werner von Green,
our leading space expert.

737
00:28:18,300 --> 00:28:21,400
- [Tom] Is this a Bergman
film all of a sudden?

738
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:23,800
- [Announcer] Stay tuned
for further bulletins.

739
00:28:23,800 --> 00:28:25,700
- Wish we had parents
instead of this radio.

740
00:28:25,700 --> 00:28:28,267
- Billy, what does
a Martian look like?

741
00:28:28,267 --> 00:28:31,033
- I dunno, nobody's
ever seen one.

742
00:28:31,033 --> 00:28:32,267
- [Joel] What's Vietnam?

743
00:28:32,267 --> 00:28:34,500
- I don't believe
there are any Martians.

744
00:28:34,500 --> 00:28:36,000
- You don't, huh?

745
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:38,333
What would you do if a Martian
walked right up behind you?

746
00:28:38,333 --> 00:28:40,033
- I'd scream.

747
00:28:40,033 --> 00:28:41,533
- Hey, how ironic!

748
00:28:41,533 --> 00:28:43,200
I'm a victim of circumstance.

749
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:46,467
- Aw, stop it, Betty,
I'm trying to sleep.

750
00:28:46,467 --> 00:28:48,067
- I see a Martian.

751
00:28:48,067 --> 00:28:48,900
♪ Hello ♪

752
00:28:48,900 --> 00:28:49,733
♪ Hello ♪

753
00:28:49,733 --> 00:28:50,567
♪ Hello ♪

754
00:28:50,567 --> 00:28:51,500
♪ Hello ♪

755
00:28:51,500 --> 00:28:52,700
- Come on, let's go home.

756
00:28:52,700 --> 00:28:54,967
- [Tom] I'll lie
there with the, huh?

757
00:28:54,967 --> 00:28:56,533
- Who, who are you?

758
00:28:56,533 --> 00:28:57,900
- We're from Mars.

759
00:28:57,900 --> 00:28:59,333
Don't be afraid.

760
00:28:59,333 --> 00:29:01,100
We have children just
like you on Mars.

761
00:29:01,100 --> 00:29:02,600
- [Joel] Only
they're worse actors.

762
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:04,967
- What are those funny things
sticking out of your heads?

763
00:29:04,967 --> 00:29:06,833
- Those are our antennae.

764
00:29:06,833 --> 00:29:08,633
- Are you a television set?

765
00:29:08,633 --> 00:29:11,000
- No, but I play one on TV.

766
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,900
- Stupid question.

767
00:29:12,900 --> 00:29:15,533
Is this what you want to
do to our children on Mars?

768
00:29:15,533 --> 00:29:17,900
Turn them into
nincompoops like these?

769
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:19,200
- Hold your tongue, Voldar.

770
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:20,667
(mumbling)

771
00:29:20,667 --> 00:29:22,067
What's your name, little boy?

772
00:29:22,067 --> 00:29:24,633
- Who's your daddy?
- Billy, Billy Foster, sir.

773
00:29:24,633 --> 00:29:27,000
And this is my sister Betty.

774
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:28,633
- Perhaps you can
help us, Billy.

775
00:29:28,633 --> 00:29:29,867
- And Betty.

776
00:29:29,867 --> 00:29:31,367
- We're looking for one
of your Santa Clauses.

777
00:29:31,367 --> 00:29:33,300
- [Billy] There's
only one Santa Claus.

778
00:29:33,300 --> 00:29:35,167
- We've seen many of
them in your cities.

779
00:29:35,167 --> 00:29:37,933
- Oh, those are his helpers.

780
00:29:37,933 --> 00:29:40,400
There's only one
real Santa Claus,

781
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:44,400
and he's in his workshop
up at the North Pole.

782
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:45,867
- That's what we came
here to find out.

783
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:48,833
- Oh great, kid, you just
fingered Kris Kringle.

784
00:29:48,833 --> 00:29:50,067
- Come on, you two.
- Let me go!

785
00:29:50,067 --> 00:29:51,000
- [Billy] Where
are you taking us?

786
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:52,500
- Leave them alone, Voldar!

787
00:29:52,500 --> 00:29:55,033
- What, and leave them here
to inform the authorities?

788
00:29:55,033 --> 00:29:56,233
- He's right, Kimar,
we better take them

789
00:29:56,233 --> 00:29:58,900
along with us to the North Pole.

790
00:30:00,667 --> 00:30:02,533
- Very well, come along.

791
00:30:02,533 --> 00:30:06,100
(dramatic music)

792
00:30:06,100 --> 00:30:08,033
- [Tom] Ooh, Maynard Ferguson
playing a ballad there.

793
00:30:08,033 --> 00:30:10,200
- This morning, two children
disappeared mysteriously

794
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:12,467
from the vicinity of Welch Lake.

795
00:30:12,467 --> 00:30:14,733
The police have found no
clues, and it seems as though

796
00:30:14,733 --> 00:30:18,333
Billy and Betty Foster have
simply vanished into thin air.

797
00:30:18,333 --> 00:30:19,667
This appears to be a
day when everything

798
00:30:19,667 --> 00:30:21,167
is vanishing into thin air.

799
00:30:21,167 --> 00:30:23,833
- Including a few
frames of the film.

800
00:30:23,833 --> 00:30:25,667
- The armed forces are
continuing their search

801
00:30:25,667 --> 00:30:27,733
for the mysterious
object from space.

802
00:30:27,733 --> 00:30:31,033
(ominous music)

803
00:30:31,033 --> 00:30:32,367
- [Tom] And now,
for your enjoyment,

804
00:30:32,367 --> 00:30:35,767
some suggestive scenes
of jets refueling.

805
00:30:38,600 --> 00:30:40,733
(gasping)

806
00:30:42,533 --> 00:30:43,800
- [Joel] All done in there?

807
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:45,100
- Why do you think
they call him Dropo?

808
00:30:45,100 --> 00:30:46,100
- All right, Billy and Betty.

809
00:30:46,100 --> 00:30:48,233
Nobody's here, come on in.

810
00:30:49,567 --> 00:30:51,033
- Golly!

811
00:30:51,033 --> 00:30:52,967
- [Tom] Uh, yeah, I pretty
much run this place.

812
00:30:52,967 --> 00:30:54,433
- Now, I'm not supposed
to bring you here.

813
00:30:54,433 --> 00:30:57,967
The chief's gonna be
awful mad if he finds us.

814
00:30:57,967 --> 00:31:00,600
- Boy, wait'll the
kids at home find out

815
00:31:00,600 --> 00:31:03,800
that I was in a real
Martian spaceship.

816
00:31:03,800 --> 00:31:05,200
- Oh, it's all about
appearances, isn't it.

817
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:07,467
- No, don't touch anything!

818
00:31:08,300 --> 00:31:09,567
Here.

819
00:31:09,567 --> 00:31:12,133
That's the
antigravity generator.

820
00:31:12,133 --> 00:31:13,000
And these--

821
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:13,967
- [Tom] Are meaningless.

822
00:31:13,967 --> 00:31:15,500
- Are the retro rockets.
- Oh.

823
00:31:15,500 --> 00:31:17,067
- Does this light up?

824
00:31:17,067 --> 00:31:20,367
- Only when radar waves
are bouncing off our ship.

825
00:31:20,367 --> 00:31:22,233
Then we put up
this radar screen.

826
00:31:22,233 --> 00:31:24,467
Then nobody can
find us in space.

827
00:31:24,467 --> 00:31:26,333
- Boy, that's pretty sharp.

828
00:31:26,333 --> 00:31:28,000
- Yep.

829
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:29,500
- What's this, Dropo?

830
00:31:29,500 --> 00:31:31,667
- Oh, that's the
elevator signal.

831
00:31:31,667 --> 00:31:33,400
That light starts
flashing when somebody's

832
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:36,300
coming up from the
navigation deck.

833
00:31:37,433 --> 00:31:38,633
- [All] Doh!

834
00:31:38,633 --> 00:31:40,667
- Wow, Liz Taylor's
wedding ring.

835
00:31:40,667 --> 00:31:42,000
- [Joel] It's the Hope Diamond.

836
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:43,467
Hoped it was real.

837
00:31:44,700 --> 00:31:46,333
- No, no no no, don't!

838
00:31:46,333 --> 00:31:47,833
There's no time for that!

839
00:31:47,833 --> 00:31:51,133
- [Joel] (laughing) Oh,
Dropo, you've done it again!

840
00:31:51,133 --> 00:31:53,667
- [Tom] You knucklenut.

841
00:31:53,667 --> 00:31:55,133
Doo da doo da doo.

842
00:31:57,167 --> 00:32:01,800
- Nothing, nothing, no kids
in the radar box, ha ha, no.

843
00:32:04,700 --> 00:32:06,400
(clearing throat)

844
00:32:06,400 --> 00:32:08,467
- [Joel] Drop 'em, Dropo.

845
00:32:10,500 --> 00:32:13,300
- Thinking of taking another
nap in the radar box, Dropo?

846
00:32:13,300 --> 00:32:14,467
- No, s-s-sir.

847
00:32:15,867 --> 00:32:17,767
As a matter of fact, I
was just looking in there

848
00:32:17,767 --> 00:32:20,567
to remind myself never
to hide in there again.

849
00:32:20,567 --> 00:32:21,567
(laughing)

850
00:32:21,567 --> 00:32:23,067
- I bet.

851
00:32:23,067 --> 00:32:25,533
- [Tom] You know, you're the
Gilligan of your time, Dropo.

852
00:32:25,533 --> 00:32:27,033
- [Rigna] Approaching
north pole.

853
00:32:27,033 --> 00:32:29,367
- Ooh, that was suspenseful.

854
00:32:30,900 --> 00:32:32,867
- I can see Santa
Claus' workshop.

855
00:32:32,867 --> 00:32:34,233
- [Tom] Rosebud.

856
00:32:34,233 --> 00:32:37,000
(imitating breaking glass)

857
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:38,800
- Let's prepare for landing.

858
00:32:38,800 --> 00:32:41,167
Hargo, set the rocket silencers.

859
00:32:41,167 --> 00:32:42,567
Dropo.

860
00:32:42,567 --> 00:32:43,833
- Yes, sir.

861
00:32:43,833 --> 00:32:44,767
- You stay aboard and
guard those children.

862
00:32:44,767 --> 00:32:45,933
(Tom laughing idiotically)

863
00:32:45,933 --> 00:32:46,500
They must not
leave the ship now.

864
00:32:46,500 --> 00:32:48,000
- Now?

865
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:50,000
- [Tom] Is the winter of
our discontent, made glo--

866
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:51,433
- What do you mean, Voldar?

867
00:32:51,433 --> 00:32:53,300
- If we take them
with us to Mars,

868
00:32:53,300 --> 00:32:56,433
Santa's disappearance
will remain a mystery.

869
00:32:56,433 --> 00:32:59,200
No one on Earth will ever
know that Santa Claus

870
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:00,867
was kidnapped by Martians.

871
00:33:00,867 --> 00:33:02,500
- [Joel] Do you realize
what you just said?

872
00:33:02,500 --> 00:33:03,500
- [Tom] I don't think so.

873
00:33:03,500 --> 00:33:05,200
- Perhaps you're right.

874
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:06,033
Dropo.

875
00:33:06,033 --> 00:33:06,967
- Drop 'em.

876
00:33:06,967 --> 00:33:08,467
- Get back to those children,

877
00:33:08,467 --> 00:33:09,400
and don't let them out of
your sight, understand?

878
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,433
- Yes, sir, I understand.

879
00:33:10,433 --> 00:33:12,433
I'll keep an eye on 'em.

880
00:33:13,533 --> 00:33:16,100
- And now Red in
The Silent Spot.

881
00:33:16,100 --> 00:33:20,433
(Tom humming lighthearted music)

882
00:33:20,433 --> 00:33:21,367
- [Tom] Oh man.

883
00:33:21,367 --> 00:33:22,867
- We've landed.

884
00:33:22,867 --> 00:33:23,667
- [Joel] I guess we'll have
to take your word for it.

885
00:33:23,667 --> 00:33:25,400
- Secure the ship.

886
00:33:25,400 --> 00:33:27,267
Lomas, you remain
on guard and have

887
00:33:27,267 --> 00:33:29,333
the ship ready for
immediate blast-off.

888
00:33:29,333 --> 00:33:30,667
- 'Cause we've landed.

889
00:33:30,667 --> 00:33:31,933
- Rigna, Hargo, Voldar.

890
00:33:31,933 --> 00:33:33,633
- [Tom] Skeeter,
Buzzbomb, Ringja.

891
00:33:33,633 --> 00:33:34,833
- Activate Torg.

892
00:33:34,833 --> 00:33:35,767
- Torg?

893
00:33:35,767 --> 00:33:37,467
- Torg, time for go to bed.

894
00:33:37,467 --> 00:33:39,800
- To capture a roly poly
little man like Santa Claus?

895
00:33:39,800 --> 00:33:41,167
We don't need Torg.

896
00:33:41,167 --> 00:33:43,600
- We won't take any chances.

897
00:33:43,600 --> 00:33:45,933
Come, nothing can stop Torg.

898
00:33:47,733 --> 00:33:48,833
- [Tom] Torg?

899
00:33:49,933 --> 00:33:53,300
- [Joel] That
one's full-figured.

900
00:33:53,300 --> 00:33:55,500
- [Tom] Come on,
Cindy, I mean, Skipper.

901
00:33:55,500 --> 00:33:56,600
Oh heck, this shot has been in

902
00:33:56,600 --> 00:33:59,067
so many sitcoms, I'm confused.

903
00:34:04,567 --> 00:34:06,567
- They're going to
kidnap Santa Claus.

904
00:34:06,567 --> 00:34:08,767
And us too.
- They came to rob Las Vegas.

905
00:34:08,767 --> 00:34:10,633
- Not if we can help it.

906
00:34:10,633 --> 00:34:13,000
We've got to get out
of here and warn Santa.

907
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:14,267
- What's a Torg?

908
00:34:14,267 --> 00:34:16,967
- I don't know, but
I'm not afraid of him.

909
00:34:16,967 --> 00:34:19,100
- Oh, he's in denial.
- He's not going to stop us.

910
00:34:19,100 --> 00:34:20,400
Come on.

911
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:21,400
Wait, Betty.

912
00:34:22,333 --> 00:34:25,067
- [Tom] I forgot
my testosterone.

913
00:34:26,267 --> 00:34:27,400
- [Joel] Now they can't watch

914
00:34:27,400 --> 00:34:28,667
Nick at Nite.
- Why did you do that?

915
00:34:28,667 --> 00:34:30,333
- If this ship
ever leaves Earth,

916
00:34:30,333 --> 00:34:32,933
they'll have the whole U.S.
Space Force after them.

917
00:34:32,933 --> 00:34:33,800
Come on.

918
00:34:33,800 --> 00:34:34,633
Wait a minute.

919
00:34:34,633 --> 00:34:36,733
- [Tom] Now what?

920
00:34:36,733 --> 00:34:41,000
- What's he gonna do, pull
the distributor cap off?

921
00:34:43,933 --> 00:34:45,200
- There.
- Come on.

922
00:34:45,200 --> 00:34:48,767
- [Tom] Kid's the
MacGyver of his time.

923
00:34:48,767 --> 00:34:51,367
(mellow music)

924
00:34:53,767 --> 00:34:55,600
(ominous music)
(bell ringing)

925
00:34:55,600 --> 00:34:59,367
- Oh, "Jacob's Ladder,"
the lost scenes.

926
00:34:59,367 --> 00:35:01,967
- [Joel] Oh, they shot this
in Minnesota in October.

927
00:35:01,967 --> 00:35:04,300
- [Tom] Got that look to it.

928
00:35:06,900 --> 00:35:09,867
- Apparently that spaceship's
a lot bigger on the inside.

929
00:35:09,867 --> 00:35:11,700
- [Tom] Like a TARDIS.

930
00:35:16,767 --> 00:35:18,900
- [Joel] Well, at least they're
dressed for the North Pole.

931
00:35:18,900 --> 00:35:21,833
- Yeah, what is
it, about 91 below?

932
00:35:24,900 --> 00:35:26,333
- [Tom] I'd say
this is symbolic of

933
00:35:26,333 --> 00:35:28,567
the unconscious of
the lower nature.

934
00:35:28,567 --> 00:35:30,800
It's very Jungian, I'd say.

935
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:38,867
(Tom humming dramatic music)

936
00:35:38,867 --> 00:35:41,367
- [Joel] Monkey
Patrol, in color.

937
00:35:41,367 --> 00:35:44,100
(wind whooshing)

938
00:35:46,367 --> 00:35:47,900
You know, these are
like cheap versions

939
00:35:47,900 --> 00:35:49,867
of the "Lost in Space" sets.

940
00:35:49,867 --> 00:35:53,000
(Tom chuckling)

941
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:54,033
- [Tom] Say!

942
00:35:54,033 --> 00:35:55,100
Oh, it's him.

943
00:35:56,867 --> 00:35:58,200
Well, still.

944
00:35:58,200 --> 00:35:59,800
- Oscar Wilde 2000.

945
00:36:01,533 --> 00:36:03,167
- This action must
take place swiftly.

946
00:36:03,167 --> 00:36:05,133
We can't afford to
make any mistakes.

947
00:36:05,133 --> 00:36:07,633
Hargo, you cover the
rear of the workshop.

948
00:36:07,633 --> 00:36:09,167
Rigna, Voldar.

949
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:11,600
- [Joel] Ringworm,
Crankcase, Lubejob.

950
00:36:11,600 --> 00:36:13,000
- I'll direct Torg.

951
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:14,800
- Voldar isn't here.

952
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:16,467
- Rigna, go up and tell Voldar--

953
00:36:16,467 --> 00:36:19,033
- [Tom] Why, Voldar,
you've been crying.

954
00:36:19,033 --> 00:36:22,333
- Voldar, this is another
one of your delaying tactics.

955
00:36:22,333 --> 00:36:24,367
You've been opposing
me at every turn,

956
00:36:24,367 --> 00:36:27,267
and now I'm warning you,
change your attitude.

957
00:36:27,267 --> 00:36:29,033
- I'm warning you,
change your attitude.

958
00:36:29,033 --> 00:36:30,567
- Are you finished, Chief?

959
00:36:30,567 --> 00:36:32,800
- Yes I am, and you will be
too, if you're not careful.

960
00:36:32,800 --> 00:36:35,367
- Oh, but I am careful, Chief.

961
00:36:35,367 --> 00:36:36,800
- [Tom] Don't call me chief!

962
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:37,800
- So careful that I
looked in on the children

963
00:36:37,800 --> 00:36:39,100
before I left the ship.

964
00:36:39,100 --> 00:36:40,567
- You stay away
from those children.

965
00:36:40,567 --> 00:36:42,133
- That will be easy to do.

966
00:36:42,133 --> 00:36:44,100
They've escaped.

967
00:36:44,100 --> 00:36:45,767
- Voldar, if this is
your idea of a joke--

968
00:36:45,767 --> 00:36:47,267
- Ask Dropo.

969
00:36:47,267 --> 00:36:48,933
- I'm funny, just ask him.
- They overheard our plans.

970
00:36:48,933 --> 00:36:50,533
At this very moment,
they're on their way

971
00:36:50,533 --> 00:36:52,367
to Santa Claus to warn him.

972
00:36:52,367 --> 00:36:53,733
- It's true, Kimar.

973
00:36:53,733 --> 00:36:54,800
Their footprints.

974
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:56,067
- Hm, child tracks.

975
00:36:56,067 --> 00:36:58,133
Two, three days old.
- We must stop them.

976
00:36:58,133 --> 00:37:00,867
Those children mustn't
reach Santa Claus!

977
00:37:00,867 --> 00:37:03,467
Follow them, I'll put
Torg on their trail.

978
00:37:03,467 --> 00:37:04,700
- [Tom] I want those kids dead,

979
00:37:04,700 --> 00:37:06,733
I want Santa's house
burned to the ground!

980
00:37:06,733 --> 00:37:09,567
- Torg, come out
of the spaceship.

981
00:37:10,600 --> 00:37:13,800
Torg, come out of the spaceship.

982
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:17,200
- [Joel] Torg, don't make
me come into that spaceship.

983
00:37:17,200 --> 00:37:19,367
(eerie music)

984
00:37:19,367 --> 00:37:22,433
- Uh, Betty, have you ever
read the book "Alive"?

985
00:37:22,433 --> 00:37:24,967
- Billy, I can't run any more.

986
00:37:24,967 --> 00:37:26,300
I'm cold.

987
00:37:26,300 --> 00:37:27,133
(hissing)

988
00:37:27,133 --> 00:37:28,233
And I'm tired.

989
00:37:28,233 --> 00:37:30,567
And it's beginning to snow.

990
00:37:30,567 --> 00:37:32,267
- [Tom] It's beginning to
look a lot like Christmas.

991
00:37:32,267 --> 00:37:34,933
- Try, we've got to warn Santa.

992
00:37:34,933 --> 00:37:36,867
We can't stop now.

993
00:37:36,867 --> 00:37:38,467
They might catch us.

994
00:37:38,467 --> 00:37:39,800
- Where is Santa?

995
00:37:39,800 --> 00:37:40,833
- Sleeping it off.

996
00:37:40,833 --> 00:37:42,067
- I don't know.

997
00:37:42,067 --> 00:37:45,667
His workshop must be
somewhere around here.

998
00:37:45,667 --> 00:37:48,967
- [Tom] All of a sudden
this is "To Build a Fire."

999
00:37:48,967 --> 00:37:50,733
- Betty, look!

1000
00:37:50,733 --> 00:37:51,733
It's Voldar!

1001
00:37:51,733 --> 00:37:52,867
- [Joel] No, that's Creamhorn

1002
00:37:52,867 --> 00:37:54,367
over there.
- He's the mean one.

1003
00:37:54,367 --> 00:37:56,667
The one who doesn't like us.

1004
00:37:56,667 --> 00:37:58,967
- Oh, who wouldn't
like you, princess?

1005
00:37:58,967 --> 00:38:00,733
- [Tom] Yeah, please.

1006
00:38:01,900 --> 00:38:05,633
- [Joel] "Ice Station
Zebra," the early years.

1007
00:38:08,833 --> 00:38:13,333
- [Tom] It looks like Eric
Heiden gone horribly wrong.

1008
00:38:19,733 --> 00:38:21,233
- Ah, watch this,
I'm flipping him off!

1009
00:38:21,233 --> 00:38:22,167
- [Tom] Sh!

1010
00:38:24,700 --> 00:38:28,700
- [Joel] What is this,
the end of "The Shining?"

1011
00:38:29,867 --> 00:38:31,433
- [Tom] Oh, you have
got to be kidding me!

1012
00:38:31,433 --> 00:38:33,367
(laughing)

1013
00:38:33,367 --> 00:38:36,567
(bear growling)

1014
00:38:36,567 --> 00:38:39,400
- Suzy Chapstick,
the early years.

1015
00:38:42,100 --> 00:38:43,900
- [Joel] Hey, check it
out, there's a stupid guy

1016
00:38:43,900 --> 00:38:47,200
in a goofy bear
costume out here!

1017
00:38:47,200 --> 00:38:48,833
- Why did he run away?

1018
00:38:48,833 --> 00:38:49,900
- [Tom] What's Vietnam?

1019
00:38:49,900 --> 00:38:51,133
- I don't know.

1020
00:38:53,933 --> 00:38:54,767
- [Betty] Uh-oh!

1021
00:38:54,767 --> 00:38:56,267
- It's Santa Bear!

1022
00:38:58,633 --> 00:39:02,100
- [Joel] Quick, in here
where we can be cornered.

1023
00:39:02,100 --> 00:39:05,133
(bear growling)

1024
00:39:05,133 --> 00:39:07,767
(Tom humming dramatic music)

1025
00:39:07,767 --> 00:39:09,933
- Ah, same to you, squirt.

1026
00:39:12,967 --> 00:39:16,467
- [Tom] I can see the head
piece draped over the body.

1027
00:39:16,467 --> 00:39:18,467
What kind of a bear?

1028
00:39:18,467 --> 00:39:19,700
- [Joel] Look,
shouldn't you be in

1029
00:39:19,700 --> 00:39:21,633
"Holiday on Ice" or something?

1030
00:39:21,633 --> 00:39:23,967
- [Tom] Allo allo allo allo.

1031
00:39:28,533 --> 00:39:29,900
- Ah, forget it.

1032
00:39:29,900 --> 00:39:32,500
(bear roaring)

1033
00:39:32,500 --> 00:39:35,067
Hm, must be an adenoid problem.

1034
00:39:36,367 --> 00:39:37,700
- Don't move, Betty.

1035
00:39:37,700 --> 00:39:39,367
I'll go take a look.

1036
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:42,833
- [Tom] I think the coast is...

1037
00:39:42,833 --> 00:39:47,833
Thunk, oh no, his head must've
gone about 75 feet, woo-hoo!

1038
00:39:47,833 --> 00:39:50,900
- It's all right
now, Betty, come on.

1039
00:39:53,233 --> 00:39:55,300
- I'm cold.
- And unfeeling.

1040
00:39:55,300 --> 00:39:57,467
- I wish it wouldn't snow.

1041
00:39:58,567 --> 00:40:00,533
- That's the best thing
that could happen.

1042
00:40:00,533 --> 00:40:01,933
It'll cover our tracks,

1043
00:40:01,933 --> 00:40:04,167
and be harder for the
Martians to find us.

1044
00:40:04,167 --> 00:40:06,900
- [Joel] And we'll freeze to
death and be little kidsicles.

1045
00:40:06,900 --> 00:40:09,600
- And it will be hard for
us to find Santa's workshop.

1046
00:40:09,600 --> 00:40:11,267
I'm scared.

1047
00:40:11,267 --> 00:40:12,733
- We'll find it.

1048
00:40:12,733 --> 00:40:14,133
Which way is north?

1049
00:40:14,133 --> 00:40:15,067
- [Tom] First we'll make contact

1050
00:40:15,067 --> 00:40:17,633
with the Norwegian underground.

1051
00:40:20,300 --> 00:40:23,467
- I see it, I see
it, Santa's workshop!

1052
00:40:23,467 --> 00:40:25,467
- [Joel] No, that's the
Children's Television Workshop.

1053
00:40:25,467 --> 00:40:26,367
- Right there!

1054
00:40:26,367 --> 00:40:27,533
See the lights?

1055
00:40:27,533 --> 00:40:28,367
- Where?

1056
00:40:29,367 --> 00:40:31,367
The lights are moving.

1057
00:40:31,367 --> 00:40:33,267
(dramatic music)

1058
00:40:33,267 --> 00:40:35,000
- [Joel] Isn't that the
"Jeopardy!" theme song

1059
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:36,533
done in a minor key?

1060
00:40:36,533 --> 00:40:37,833
(humming ominous music)

1061
00:40:37,833 --> 00:40:40,733
- They're coming towards us.

1062
00:40:40,733 --> 00:40:42,667
- Betty, that's
not Santa's house.

1063
00:40:42,667 --> 00:40:45,133
- [Tom] That's my wife,
ba-boom, thank you.

1064
00:40:45,133 --> 00:40:46,400
- [Betty] What is it?

1065
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:47,433
- [Joel] It's a guy
in a cardboard box

1066
00:40:47,433 --> 00:40:49,900
with a coffee urn on his head.

1067
00:40:51,633 --> 00:40:53,333
- Hey, it's the robot
that walked from Hawaii

1068
00:40:53,333 --> 00:40:55,033
to Gilligan's Island.

1069
00:40:57,200 --> 00:40:59,467
- [Joel] What a
dopey-looking robot, man.

1070
00:40:59,467 --> 00:41:03,300
The polar bear was a
lot better than that.

1071
00:41:03,300 --> 00:41:04,733
- Booth or table?

1072
00:41:06,733 --> 00:41:08,500
- [Tom] It was after
the apocalypse.

1073
00:41:08,500 --> 00:41:12,167
No one was prepared for
the robot holocaust.

1074
00:41:14,333 --> 00:41:17,533
- [Joel] Aw, come here,
ya little ragamuffins, ah.

1075
00:41:17,533 --> 00:41:19,700
- Now destroy them, crush them!

1076
00:41:19,700 --> 00:41:21,100
- You were adopted.
- Crush them, Torg!

1077
00:41:21,100 --> 00:41:22,100
Do as I say!

1078
00:41:23,267 --> 00:41:25,633
- Voldar, I knew you'd
try something like this.

1079
00:41:25,633 --> 00:41:28,233
I set Torg's controls
so he will obey only me.

1080
00:41:28,233 --> 00:41:29,533
Release them, Torg!

1081
00:41:29,533 --> 00:41:32,100
- Oil can, oil can!
- You are very lucky.

1082
00:41:32,100 --> 00:41:34,233
Now don't try to escape again.

1083
00:41:34,233 --> 00:41:36,100
You may not be so
lucky next time.

1084
00:41:36,100 --> 00:41:37,700
Hargo, take them
back to the ship,

1085
00:41:37,700 --> 00:41:40,467
lock them up, and rejoin us.

1086
00:41:40,467 --> 00:41:44,100
- You won't get away with
this, you, you Martians!

1087
00:41:44,100 --> 00:41:45,600
- Santa's gonna cut you, man!

1088
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:47,700
Santa's a blade man, man!

1089
00:41:47,700 --> 00:41:49,000
- The danger grows

1090
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:50,267
with every minute.
- As does my love.

1091
00:41:50,267 --> 00:41:51,967
- Let's get Santa
Claus and blast off.

1092
00:41:51,967 --> 00:41:55,167
We'll surround the workshop
and send Torg in to get Santa.

1093
00:41:55,167 --> 00:41:57,300
Nobody is to be harmed
unless they get in our way.

1094
00:41:57,300 --> 00:41:58,200
- Bah.

1095
00:41:58,200 --> 00:41:59,233
- [All] Humbug.

1096
00:41:59,233 --> 00:42:00,867
- No one is to be harmed.

1097
00:42:00,867 --> 00:42:04,267
What has happened to the
great warriors of our planet?

1098
00:42:04,267 --> 00:42:06,433
Mars used to be
the planet of war!

1099
00:42:06,433 --> 00:42:07,633
- [Tom] War, huh,

1100
00:42:07,633 --> 00:42:09,500
what is it good for?
- Mark my words, Kimar.

1101
00:42:09,500 --> 00:42:11,767
Your softness will destroy us.

1102
00:42:11,767 --> 00:42:13,967
- [Joel] Your Downy softness.

1103
00:42:13,967 --> 00:42:16,267
- Santa Claus, toys,
games, laughing children.

1104
00:42:16,267 --> 00:42:17,933
- Well, we shall see.

1105
00:42:17,933 --> 00:42:19,733
But for now, to your posts!

1106
00:42:19,733 --> 00:42:21,400
- VFW Post 309!

1107
00:42:21,400 --> 00:42:22,867
- Torg, follow me!

1108
00:42:22,867 --> 00:42:24,600
(dramatic music)

1109
00:42:24,600 --> 00:42:26,100
- [Tom] Walk this way!

1110
00:42:26,100 --> 00:42:27,133
- If I could walk that way, I
wouldn't be wearing the box.

1111
00:42:27,133 --> 00:42:28,467
- [Tom] Ba-bing!

1112
00:42:29,700 --> 00:42:32,300
(all shouting)

1113
00:42:34,033 --> 00:42:35,200
- [Joel] What does that say,

1114
00:42:35,200 --> 00:42:37,967
"No shirt, no
shoes, no service?"

1115
00:42:37,967 --> 00:42:40,700
- [Tom] (chuckling)
Smoke free my Aunt Fanny!

1116
00:42:40,700 --> 00:42:42,033
Ho ho ho!

1117
00:42:42,033 --> 00:42:43,667
- Get him, Torg.

1118
00:42:43,667 --> 00:42:46,167
- Exterminate with
extreme prejudice!

1119
00:42:46,167 --> 00:42:49,300
- [Tom] Whoa, we're outta here.

1120
00:42:49,300 --> 00:42:51,033
- [Joel] Knock knock.

1121
00:42:58,700 --> 00:43:01,267
(mellow music)

1122
00:43:03,833 --> 00:43:06,433
- Man, this "Santa Claus
Conquers the Martians"

1123
00:43:06,433 --> 00:43:08,200
is really depressing.

1124
00:43:08,200 --> 00:43:12,067
It makes it really feel
like Christmas, ho ho no.

1125
00:43:12,067 --> 00:43:14,833
- Yeah, I feel jolly,
just like old St. Nick.

1126
00:43:14,833 --> 00:43:16,333
Ho ho ho ho ho ho.

1127
00:43:17,567 --> 00:43:19,067
- Ricky, get me a scotch,

1128
00:43:19,067 --> 00:43:21,267
I'm suffering from
Christmas depression!

1129
00:43:21,267 --> 00:43:22,800
- Hey, you guys.

1130
00:43:22,800 --> 00:43:24,167
- Joel, Joel, couldn't we
see a more cheerful movie,

1131
00:43:24,167 --> 00:43:25,600
like maybe "The
Sorrow and the Pity"?

1132
00:43:25,600 --> 00:43:27,667
- Well, I got that
all covered, you guys.

1133
00:43:27,667 --> 00:43:31,667
I tricked Frank into sending
up a bunch of movies up here.

1134
00:43:31,667 --> 00:43:32,900
- Wow!
- And it's something

1135
00:43:32,900 --> 00:43:34,367
we can watch after
the experiment.

1136
00:43:34,367 --> 00:43:37,200
Let's see, we got "Grinch
Who Stole Christmas."

1137
00:43:37,200 --> 00:43:39,167
- Are you sure that's not "The
Fish Who Saved Pittsburgh?"

1138
00:43:39,167 --> 00:43:40,967
- Yes, my little
huckleberry friend.

1139
00:43:40,967 --> 00:43:43,700
We also got "Mr. Magoo's
Christmas Carol."

1140
00:43:43,700 --> 00:43:45,833
- No, Jim Backus lives!

1141
00:43:45,833 --> 00:43:47,767
- And "Frosty the Snowman."

1142
00:43:47,767 --> 00:43:50,067
- "Frosty the Snowman", Jackie
Vernon did not die in vain!

1143
00:43:50,067 --> 00:43:51,267
(cheering)

1144
00:43:51,267 --> 00:43:52,600
- Right, we've got Rankin Bass'

1145
00:43:52,600 --> 00:43:54,100
"Rudolph the
Red-Nosed Reindeer."

1146
00:43:54,100 --> 00:43:56,100
- All right, Burl Ives died
so that we may enjoy the--

1147
00:43:56,100 --> 00:43:58,267
- Hey, uh, he's not dead.

1148
00:43:58,267 --> 00:43:59,800
- Oh, sorry, Burl.

1149
00:43:59,800 --> 00:44:01,567
- Yeah, and then we've got
"A Charlie Brown Christmas."

1150
00:44:01,567 --> 00:44:03,967
- Oh boy, I love that
one, especially the part

1151
00:44:03,967 --> 00:44:05,767
where they eat all those
Dolly Madison cakes.

1152
00:44:05,767 --> 00:44:08,500
You know, Koo Koos,
Zingers, Razzies.

1153
00:44:08,500 --> 00:44:11,033
- Wait a second, wait a minute.

1154
00:44:11,033 --> 00:44:13,000
Those were the commercials.

1155
00:44:13,000 --> 00:44:15,067
Actually, without the
Dolly Madison commercials,

1156
00:44:15,067 --> 00:44:18,467
the entire show is about
nine minutes long, okay?

1157
00:44:18,467 --> 00:44:20,267
We got a few others here.

1158
00:44:20,267 --> 00:44:22,567
We've got "It's a
Wonderful Life."

1159
00:44:22,567 --> 00:44:24,533
- Wow, really great!
- I love that one!

1160
00:44:24,533 --> 00:44:26,367
- Well, don't get too excited,

1161
00:44:26,367 --> 00:44:28,933
it's the lame Marlo
Thomas version.

1162
00:44:28,933 --> 00:44:30,500
- Shame on you, Marlo.

1163
00:44:30,500 --> 00:44:32,167
- We also got "Miracle
on 34th Street."

1164
00:44:32,167 --> 00:44:33,467
(cheering)

1165
00:44:33,467 --> 00:44:35,667
No, no, it's the
David Hartman one.

1166
00:44:35,667 --> 00:44:37,600
- Shame on you guys.

1167
00:44:37,600 --> 00:44:38,867
- We got a few
others here, though,

1168
00:44:38,867 --> 00:44:40,767
it's kinda going to the
bottom of the bag here,

1169
00:44:40,767 --> 00:44:42,100
kind of some low-budget ones.

1170
00:44:42,100 --> 00:44:44,967
"The Christmas that
Totally Ruled,"

1171
00:44:44,967 --> 00:44:47,467
it's about a
curmudgeonly old man

1172
00:44:47,467 --> 00:44:50,033
that learns the true
meaning of Christmas.

1173
00:44:50,033 --> 00:44:51,267
- Fresh idea!

1174
00:44:51,267 --> 00:44:52,433
- We have "The Christmas
That Wasn't That Bad,"

1175
00:44:52,433 --> 00:44:54,067
which is about a
curmudgeonly old woman

1176
00:44:54,067 --> 00:44:55,933
who learns the true
meaning of Christmas.

1177
00:44:55,933 --> 00:44:58,567
And then there's "The Christmas
That Really Kicked Ass,"

1178
00:44:58,567 --> 00:45:00,367
which is about a
curmudgeonly old man

1179
00:45:00,367 --> 00:45:01,933
and a curmudgeonly
old woman that learns

1180
00:45:01,933 --> 00:45:03,200
the true meaning of Christmas.

1181
00:45:03,200 --> 00:45:04,033
- Oh, that would be--
(alarm buzzing)

1182
00:45:04,033 --> 00:45:05,433
- Ah, we got movie sign!

1183
00:45:05,433 --> 00:45:08,000
(all shouting)

1184
00:45:15,967 --> 00:45:18,133
- [Tom] Now we've gotta
come back and watch this?

1185
00:45:18,133 --> 00:45:19,533
- [Joel] Oh boy.

1186
00:45:19,533 --> 00:45:20,700
- Sorry, we just waxed.

1187
00:45:20,700 --> 00:45:22,267
- No one's allowed

1188
00:45:22,267 --> 00:45:24,000
- [Joel] My spine!
(imitating cracking)

1189
00:45:24,000 --> 00:45:27,200
- [Santa] You're the
biggest toy I've ever seen!

1190
00:45:27,200 --> 00:45:30,133
- [Tom] I could
use a toy like you.

1191
00:45:30,133 --> 00:45:30,967
Ah.

1192
00:45:31,933 --> 00:45:33,867
- And very well-made, too.

1193
00:45:33,867 --> 00:45:36,233
- [Tom] Nice ash can.

1194
00:45:36,233 --> 00:45:39,933
- By the great dog star,
Santa's treating him like a toy!

1195
00:45:39,933 --> 00:45:41,600
- [Joel] Oh, he treats
everyone like that.

1196
00:45:41,600 --> 00:45:43,833
- Get him, Torg, grab him!

1197
00:45:43,833 --> 00:45:46,067
- He's become a toy.

1198
00:45:46,067 --> 00:45:48,300
- Rigna, we'll have to
get Santa ourselves.

1199
00:45:48,300 --> 00:45:49,267
Come on, Voldar.

1200
00:45:49,267 --> 00:45:51,867
(suspenseful music)

1201
00:45:51,867 --> 00:45:55,233
- [Tom] Nobody expects
the Spanish Inquisition!

1202
00:45:55,233 --> 00:45:56,600
- What have we here?

1203
00:45:56,600 --> 00:45:58,133
More toys?

1204
00:45:58,133 --> 00:45:59,467
- Those are Martians!

1205
00:45:59,467 --> 00:46:00,967
- Santa Claus, you're
coming with us.

1206
00:46:00,967 --> 00:46:02,567
- [Joel] You're coming to town.

1207
00:46:02,567 --> 00:46:03,633
- No, you can't take him now!

1208
00:46:03,633 --> 00:46:04,733
It's too near Christmas!

1209
00:46:04,733 --> 00:46:05,567
- Quiet, you.

1210
00:46:05,567 --> 00:46:06,400
- But.

1211
00:46:07,700 --> 00:46:10,200
- [Joel] Oh, he
stopped them short.

1212
00:46:10,200 --> 00:46:13,033
- We don't want to
hurt you, Santa Claus,

1213
00:46:13,033 --> 00:46:14,500
so come along quietly.

1214
00:46:14,500 --> 00:46:17,100
- How are you gonna hurt
him with a hair dryer?

1215
00:46:17,100 --> 00:46:18,233
- [Joel] Hey, lawn jockey.

1216
00:46:18,233 --> 00:46:19,167
Just kidding.

1217
00:46:19,167 --> 00:46:20,000
- Why?

1218
00:46:21,633 --> 00:46:24,567
Why did you have to
do that to my helpers?

1219
00:46:24,567 --> 00:46:27,000
- It's harmless, it will
wear off in a short while.

1220
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:28,933
- [Tom] It's just a
Wham-O Air Blaster.

1221
00:46:28,933 --> 00:46:32,967
- Well, why didn't you
say so in the first place?

1222
00:46:32,967 --> 00:46:34,167
- Now, you come with us.

1223
00:46:34,167 --> 00:46:35,833
We need you on Mars.

1224
00:46:38,067 --> 00:46:39,900
- Noonan!
- You moved.

1225
00:46:42,833 --> 00:46:44,033
Hm.

1226
00:46:44,033 --> 00:46:46,333
- Are you sure this is harmless?

1227
00:46:46,333 --> 00:46:49,933
- Oh, I never saw
such lazy people.

1228
00:46:49,933 --> 00:46:51,900
Standing around like statues.

1229
00:46:51,900 --> 00:46:54,100
There's work to be done!

1230
00:46:54,100 --> 00:46:56,133
Let's get to it.

1231
00:46:56,133 --> 00:46:58,167
- [Tom] The Twilight Zone.

1232
00:46:58,167 --> 00:47:00,533
- Oh me oh my, oh me, oh my.

1233
00:47:01,767 --> 00:47:03,267
- [Tom] Down by the bayou.

1234
00:47:03,267 --> 00:47:07,367
- Mrs. Claus is going to
be very angry about this.

1235
00:47:07,367 --> 00:47:10,600
- She's gonna hit me
with a frying pan.

1236
00:47:10,600 --> 00:47:12,000
- Torg, take him!

1237
00:47:13,133 --> 00:47:15,133
Obey my commands!

1238
00:47:15,133 --> 00:47:16,167
- Forget it, Kimar.

1239
00:47:16,167 --> 00:47:17,367
- [Tom] He's not house trained.

1240
00:47:17,367 --> 00:47:18,733
- Rigna was right.

1241
00:47:18,733 --> 00:47:21,667
He's nothing but a toy now.

1242
00:47:21,667 --> 00:47:24,100
Best to leave him here.

1243
00:47:24,100 --> 00:47:28,233
- Believe me, I had nothing
whatsoever to do about this.

1244
00:47:28,233 --> 00:47:29,467
- Oh, that's what you always say

1245
00:47:29,467 --> 00:47:31,767
when you're drinking
with your friends.

1246
00:47:31,767 --> 00:47:36,767
- I can't recall a time when
you were so silent for so long.

1247
00:47:37,500 --> 00:47:39,000
- Let's go, old man!

1248
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:42,933
- Old man, take a look at my
elf, I'm a lot like you, woo!

1249
00:47:42,933 --> 00:47:46,067
(dramatic music)

1250
00:47:46,067 --> 00:47:47,600
- [Joel] Next week
on "Barnaby Jones,"

1251
00:47:47,600 --> 00:47:49,433
"Mrs. Claus of Death."

1252
00:47:52,467 --> 00:47:54,533
(gasping)

1253
00:47:54,533 --> 00:47:58,833
- [Tom] Village Voice,
Santa's Outing, what?

1254
00:47:58,833 --> 00:48:01,067
- And Mrs. Santa Claus
has positively identified

1255
00:48:01,067 --> 00:48:03,200
the kidnappers as Martians.

1256
00:48:03,200 --> 00:48:04,667
Never in the history
of mankind have

1257
00:48:04,667 --> 00:48:06,233
the nations of the
world reacted with such

1258
00:48:06,233 --> 00:48:07,933
unanimity and cooperation.

1259
00:48:07,933 --> 00:48:09,500
Tonight, the lights
will burn until dawn

1260
00:48:09,500 --> 00:48:11,867
in the United Nations building,
as the leaders of the world

1261
00:48:11,867 --> 00:48:13,233
map a course of action.

1262
00:48:13,233 --> 00:48:14,967
- [Joel] Give
sanctions more time!

1263
00:48:14,967 --> 00:48:18,000
- And, at Cape Kennedy, our
correspondent interviewed

1264
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:20,333
Werner Von Green,
the man in charge.

1265
00:48:20,333 --> 00:48:22,300
- I'm innocent, I was
only following orders!

1266
00:48:22,300 --> 00:48:23,467
Oh. (imitating cracking)
- Mr. Von Green,

1267
00:48:23,467 --> 00:48:26,400
what is the Space
Agency doing about this?

1268
00:48:26,400 --> 00:48:28,800
- Well, they have mobilized
all the men and equipment

1269
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:30,267
in our starship project.

1270
00:48:30,267 --> 00:48:32,467
- [Joel] What is that,
the Groucho duck up there?

1271
00:48:32,467 --> 00:48:34,000
- And we have rushed
our astronauts into

1272
00:48:34,000 --> 00:48:35,600
an intensive program for the
final phase of our training.

1273
00:48:35,600 --> 00:48:37,400
♪ Boom shadow, boom shadow ♪

1274
00:48:37,400 --> 00:48:38,800
- Our starship is
supposed to undergo

1275
00:48:38,800 --> 00:48:40,700
six months of test flights,
but we are going to

1276
00:48:40,700 --> 00:48:45,700
forget about the testing and
go after those Martian monkeys.

1277
00:48:46,567 --> 00:48:47,800
- [Announcer] Isn't that risky?

1278
00:48:47,800 --> 00:48:49,133
- [Tom] It will not be
difficult, Mein Fuhrer!

1279
00:48:49,133 --> 00:48:50,733
- But every one of
our astronauts is

1280
00:48:50,733 --> 00:48:54,367
begging for the chance
to go after the Martians.

1281
00:48:54,367 --> 00:48:56,067
Who wouldn't give everything

1282
00:48:56,067 --> 00:48:58,733
to bring Santa back
to our children?

1283
00:48:58,733 --> 00:49:00,467
- Me!
- Over here!

1284
00:49:00,467 --> 00:49:04,067
(suspenseful music)

1285
00:49:04,067 --> 00:49:06,967
- [Tom] Hi, I'm Bonnie at NASA.

1286
00:49:06,967 --> 00:49:08,167
- Before this decade is out,

1287
00:49:08,167 --> 00:49:10,567
we will bring Santa
back from Mars.

1288
00:49:10,567 --> 00:49:11,500
- [Tom] Remember this one?

1289
00:49:11,500 --> 00:49:13,100
"I said lunch, not launch!"

1290
00:49:13,100 --> 00:49:14,800
- Oh, "Far Out Space Nuts."

1291
00:49:14,800 --> 00:49:15,633
- Yeah.

1292
00:49:17,833 --> 00:49:20,100
- "Capricorn One" will
return after this.

1293
00:49:20,100 --> 00:49:22,533
(Tom humming lively music)

1294
00:49:22,533 --> 00:49:25,200
- [Joel] So it, uh, just
keeps going up like that, huh.

1295
00:49:25,200 --> 00:49:26,367
- Yep.
- Mm-hm.

1296
00:49:27,567 --> 00:49:30,300
- Fat bald men are
quickly mobilized.

1297
00:49:30,300 --> 00:49:33,367
- [Joel] So really,
that's really just,

1298
00:49:33,367 --> 00:49:34,967
kinda keeps heading for the sky.

1299
00:49:34,967 --> 00:49:36,967
- [Tom] That's pretty
much what it does, yeah.

1300
00:49:36,967 --> 00:49:40,200
- [Joel] Just keeps, onward
and upward like that.

1301
00:49:40,200 --> 00:49:42,033
- [Tom] Ooh, three
stars by her name.

1302
00:49:42,033 --> 00:49:43,767
Earth girls are easy.

1303
00:49:43,767 --> 00:49:46,400
- Earth hasn't reacted yet.

1304
00:49:46,400 --> 00:49:49,233
- No radar beams being
bounced off our ship.

1305
00:49:49,233 --> 00:49:52,167
Looks like we made
a clean getaway.

1306
00:49:53,033 --> 00:49:54,533
(laughing)

1307
00:49:54,533 --> 00:49:57,000
- Here I sit, broken, which
one of you clowns wrote that?

1308
00:49:57,000 --> 00:49:58,667
- He's having the
time of his life.

1309
00:49:58,667 --> 00:50:00,667
He's such a funny little man.

1310
00:50:00,667 --> 00:50:02,300
Why, I've only been with
him for five minutes,

1311
00:50:02,300 --> 00:50:05,333
and he has me laughing
just like an Earthling.

1312
00:50:05,333 --> 00:50:08,333
What's soft and round,
and you put it on a stick,

1313
00:50:08,333 --> 00:50:10,000
and you toast it in a fire?

1314
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:11,267
- [Tom] An elf?

1315
00:50:11,267 --> 00:50:12,400
- And it's green.
- Oh, a dead elf.

1316
00:50:12,400 --> 00:50:14,000
- I don't know, what?

1317
00:50:14,000 --> 00:50:15,467
- A Martianmallow!

1318
00:50:15,467 --> 00:50:17,733
(laughing)

1319
00:50:19,200 --> 00:50:20,833
- [Joel] You just heard that?

1320
00:50:20,833 --> 00:50:22,000
Geez.

1321
00:50:22,000 --> 00:50:24,000
- That's what
you're all becoming.

1322
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:25,267
Martianmallows.

1323
00:50:26,267 --> 00:50:27,200
Soft.

1324
00:50:27,200 --> 00:50:28,033
- Absorbent.

1325
00:50:28,033 --> 00:50:29,367
- Weak.

1326
00:50:29,367 --> 00:50:32,233
That old man is a menace.

1327
00:50:32,233 --> 00:50:34,600
- [Santa] And it was a
very foggy Christmas Eve.

1328
00:50:34,600 --> 00:50:37,400
- [Tom] So it was '69, I
was stationed in Phnom Penh.

1329
00:50:37,400 --> 00:50:39,433
Charlie had us
pinned down the way.

1330
00:50:39,433 --> 00:50:41,233
The only thing that kept
me going was Laotian gold

1331
00:50:41,233 --> 00:50:42,700
we got in Saigon.

1332
00:50:42,700 --> 00:50:46,500
- I tell you, it was the biggest
chimney I'd ever been in.

1333
00:50:46,500 --> 00:50:48,000
And then suddenly--

1334
00:50:48,000 --> 00:50:49,500
- [Joel] Suddenly Sally.

1335
00:50:49,500 --> 00:50:53,567
- Suddenly I realized it
wasn't a chimney at all.

1336
00:50:53,567 --> 00:50:56,633
It was the smokestack
of the Queen Elizabeth.

1337
00:50:56,633 --> 00:50:57,533
- [Tom] Ha.

1338
00:50:59,000 --> 00:51:01,000
Santa, you're just about
as funny as a train wreck.

1339
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:02,933
- Don't you think
that was funny?

1340
00:51:02,933 --> 00:51:04,133
- [Betty and Billy] Yes, Santa.

1341
00:51:04,133 --> 00:51:05,733
- [Joel] It's just
that we're Norwegian.

1342
00:51:05,733 --> 00:51:07,467
- Well, why didn't you laugh?

1343
00:51:07,467 --> 00:51:09,333
- Gee, Santa, it's
all our fault.

1344
00:51:09,333 --> 00:51:10,900
We told them where to find you.

1345
00:51:10,900 --> 00:51:13,933
- Oh, balderdash and
a fiddle-dee-dee.

1346
00:51:13,933 --> 00:51:15,967
- Whoa, language,
Santa, language!

1347
00:51:15,967 --> 00:51:18,067
- Everybody knows
where Santa lives.

1348
00:51:18,067 --> 00:51:21,567
Besides, I've always
wanted to visit Mars.

1349
00:51:21,567 --> 00:51:23,733
(all laughing idiotically)

1350
00:51:23,733 --> 00:51:25,733
- Mommy and Daddy are
going to be angry.

1351
00:51:25,733 --> 00:51:27,433
- You think that's something?

1352
00:51:27,433 --> 00:51:29,867
I can just see Mrs. Claus now.

1353
00:51:29,867 --> 00:51:32,100
Christmas coming,
and I'm not there.

1354
00:51:32,100 --> 00:51:33,600
She'll have a fit.

1355
00:51:33,600 --> 00:51:36,367
- The elves have learned
how to handle her, though.

1356
00:51:36,367 --> 00:51:38,100
- Oh me oh my oh me.

1357
00:51:38,100 --> 00:51:39,667
- [Tom] By the bayou.

1358
00:51:39,667 --> 00:51:42,067
- Come and get it, dinnertime!

1359
00:51:42,067 --> 00:51:43,700
- Here's Dropo!

1360
00:51:43,700 --> 00:51:46,433
If I can't cheer
you up, Dropo can.

1361
00:51:46,433 --> 00:51:48,467
He always makes me laugh.

1362
00:51:48,467 --> 00:51:51,333
- You'll have a
wonderful dinner tonight.

1363
00:51:51,333 --> 00:51:54,733
Oh, there's soup,
and, and beef stew,

1364
00:51:54,733 --> 00:51:57,067
and chocolate ice cream.

1365
00:51:57,067 --> 00:51:58,967
- And Spam?
- No thank you, Dropo.

1366
00:51:58,967 --> 00:52:00,267
I'm not hungry.

1367
00:52:00,267 --> 00:52:02,133
- Come on, Billy.

1368
00:52:02,133 --> 00:52:04,767
Ooh, well, is it all right if

1369
00:52:04,767 --> 00:52:07,300
I have your chocolate ice cream?

1370
00:52:07,300 --> 00:52:08,533
- Sure.

1371
00:52:08,533 --> 00:52:11,033
- Oh, I just love
chocolate ice cream.

1372
00:52:11,033 --> 00:52:12,400
- [Joel] You know,
that Dropo plays it

1373
00:52:12,400 --> 00:52:14,400
a little broader
than Larry Storch.

1374
00:52:14,400 --> 00:52:16,033
- Yep.
- Mm-hm.

1375
00:52:16,033 --> 00:52:17,267
What a pig he is.

1376
00:52:17,267 --> 00:52:21,200
- Gee, Mars must be a
terrible place to live.

1377
00:52:21,200 --> 00:52:23,867
Some chocolate ice cream.

1378
00:52:23,867 --> 00:52:25,267
- Pills for dinner!

1379
00:52:25,267 --> 00:52:27,867
- Ho ho, what are
we, Judy Garland?

1380
00:52:27,867 --> 00:52:29,967
- I suppose if a
Martian has a headache,

1381
00:52:29,967 --> 00:52:33,600
he doesn't take pills, he
takes chocolate ice cream.

1382
00:52:33,600 --> 00:52:35,967
- [Joel] Ah, that's
not too funny, Santa.

1383
00:52:35,967 --> 00:52:37,200
You're getting a light.

1384
00:52:37,200 --> 00:52:38,633
- Oh dear, oh dear.

1385
00:52:38,633 --> 00:52:39,700
- [Tom] You've been
a great audience.

1386
00:52:39,700 --> 00:52:41,200
- Kimar, look at this!

1387
00:52:41,200 --> 00:52:43,600
That small blip is not an
asteroid, it's a spaceship,

1388
00:52:43,600 --> 00:52:45,000
and it's on our tail.

1389
00:52:45,000 --> 00:52:46,133
It's getting closer.

1390
00:52:46,133 --> 00:52:47,633
- Impossible, Rigna.

1391
00:52:47,633 --> 00:52:50,000
They couldn't have spotted us,
we have our radar shield on.

1392
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:52,900
- I know that, sir, but
they are gaining on us.

1393
00:52:52,900 --> 00:52:54,700
- Is it possible Earth
has a secret device

1394
00:52:54,700 --> 00:52:56,533
that can penetrate
our radar shield?

1395
00:52:56,533 --> 00:53:00,367
- They have a secret device,
and his name is Billy Foster.

1396
00:53:00,367 --> 00:53:03,333
- [Tom] Billy Foster
is The Secret Device.

1397
00:53:03,333 --> 00:53:05,133
- They'll destroy
us if we allow them!

1398
00:53:05,133 --> 00:53:06,867
- [Joel] Oh, adjust
your sash, Carl.

1399
00:53:06,867 --> 00:53:08,367
- I won't allow it.

1400
00:53:08,367 --> 00:53:10,433
- Oh no, he's gonna sing!

1401
00:53:13,067 --> 00:53:14,567
- [Tom] Ugh, yuck.

1402
00:53:14,567 --> 00:53:16,600
- I think we underestimate
the resourcefulness

1403
00:53:16,600 --> 00:53:17,800
of these Earth people.

1404
00:53:17,800 --> 00:53:18,733
- [Tom] I sure hope
that's pudding.

1405
00:53:18,733 --> 00:53:20,767
- Very clever of the boy.

1406
00:53:20,767 --> 00:53:22,267
Make your repairs, Rigna.

1407
00:53:22,267 --> 00:53:24,867
I'll take evasive action.

1408
00:53:24,867 --> 00:53:27,100
- [Joel] Time for some fun.

1409
00:53:29,467 --> 00:53:30,700
- Well.

1410
00:53:30,700 --> 00:53:31,933
- [Tom] Thunk, ooh!

1411
00:53:31,933 --> 00:53:36,000
- How is Santa, and
the little Earthlings?

1412
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:39,100
My, it must be tiresome,
cooped up in this little room.

1413
00:53:39,100 --> 00:53:40,900
- Yeah, but it's
only $18 a night.

1414
00:53:40,900 --> 00:53:43,733
- Say, how would you like
to see the rest of the ship?

1415
00:53:43,733 --> 00:53:44,967
- [Joel] Bite me.

1416
00:53:44,967 --> 00:53:47,300
- You're not fooling
me, you don't like us.

1417
00:53:47,300 --> 00:53:48,767
- You're mean.

1418
00:53:48,767 --> 00:53:51,367
- Oh, come on, now,
that's not true.

1419
00:53:51,367 --> 00:53:52,767
- [Tom] Well.

1420
00:53:52,767 --> 00:53:55,767
- Why, Santa makes everyone
feel good, even me.

1421
00:53:55,767 --> 00:53:57,067
- I don't trust you.

1422
00:53:57,067 --> 00:53:58,833
- Now now, Billy boy.

1423
00:53:58,833 --> 00:54:00,133
- Grease him, Santa!

1424
00:54:00,133 --> 00:54:01,633
- That's not the
Christmas spirit.

1425
00:54:01,633 --> 00:54:03,900
- Ah, I'm Jewish, Santa.
- Why, of course, Voldar.

1426
00:54:03,900 --> 00:54:07,167
We'd love to take
the grand tour.

1427
00:54:07,167 --> 00:54:10,300
- [Tom] Follow my lead,
Billy, I'm packin' heat.

1428
00:54:10,300 --> 00:54:13,400
- [Joel] I want to
be alone with Santa.

1429
00:54:13,400 --> 00:54:15,933
- [Tom] Nice take to
the camera, thank you.

1430
00:54:15,933 --> 00:54:17,000
What a clown.

1431
00:54:18,433 --> 00:54:20,267
- [Joel] Oh, that must be
the laundry cute over there.

1432
00:54:20,267 --> 00:54:23,100
- [Tom] Why are
things in English?

1433
00:54:26,233 --> 00:54:27,733
- This room is called the--
- Air lock.

1434
00:54:27,733 --> 00:54:28,733
- [Joel] Same to you, woodleg!

1435
00:54:28,733 --> 00:54:29,933
- That's right.

1436
00:54:29,933 --> 00:54:31,200
- Sure, this is
where you come when

1437
00:54:31,200 --> 00:54:33,433
you're ready to go out in space.

1438
00:54:33,433 --> 00:54:34,533
It's airtight.

1439
00:54:34,533 --> 00:54:36,367
You put on your space suit,

1440
00:54:36,367 --> 00:54:38,033
and go out through that door.

1441
00:54:38,033 --> 00:54:39,233
- So if you wanted
to kill somebody,

1442
00:54:39,233 --> 00:54:41,033
send 'em out, ahh!

1443
00:54:41,033 --> 00:54:44,267
- And they pump air back
into the room through there.

1444
00:54:44,267 --> 00:54:46,733
When it reaches the pressure
of the rest of the ship,

1445
00:54:46,733 --> 00:54:48,400
you can take your
space suit off.

1446
00:54:48,400 --> 00:54:50,700
- [Tom] Who is this kid,
Ira Flatow all of a sudden?

1447
00:54:50,700 --> 00:54:52,700
- Where is the control
that opens the door, sir?

1448
00:54:52,700 --> 00:54:53,633
- Not here.

1449
00:54:53,633 --> 00:54:55,667
That's in the control deck.

1450
00:54:55,667 --> 00:54:59,933
You see, once you pull that
switch, the warning bell sounds,

1451
00:54:59,933 --> 00:55:02,900
and in 60 seconds,
that door opens.

1452
00:55:02,900 --> 00:55:04,367
- That's to give a
space man a chance

1453
00:55:04,367 --> 00:55:07,000
to make a final checkup
on their equipment.

1454
00:55:07,000 --> 00:55:09,233
There's no air out in space.

1455
00:55:09,233 --> 00:55:11,100
If that door were open now,

1456
00:55:11,100 --> 00:55:14,567
it would pull all the air out
of this room, and us with it.

1457
00:55:14,567 --> 00:55:15,867
- [Voldar] You certainly
know a great deal

1458
00:55:15,867 --> 00:55:17,367
about space travel, son.

1459
00:55:17,367 --> 00:55:22,367
- [Joel] I like you, that's
why I'm going to kill you last.

1460
00:55:23,233 --> 00:55:24,733
- Maybe sooner than that.

1461
00:55:24,733 --> 00:55:26,000
(gasping)

1462
00:55:26,000 --> 00:55:27,933
(Tom laughing evilly)

1463
00:55:27,933 --> 00:55:30,233
- [Joel] I'm gone,
presto, va-voom.

1464
00:55:30,233 --> 00:55:32,333
- Santa, that clock's stopped.

1465
00:55:32,333 --> 00:55:35,767
- 60 seconds, that
must be the door timer.

1466
00:55:35,767 --> 00:55:38,400
- Have you two ever
seen a grown man scream?

1467
00:55:38,400 --> 00:55:40,133
Santa's gonna whimper
like a whipped pup.

1468
00:55:40,133 --> 00:55:41,367
- Santa, he locked us in!

1469
00:55:41,367 --> 00:55:42,700
- Oh, I don't think so.

1470
00:55:42,700 --> 00:55:45,433
He probably just stepped
out for a moment.

1471
00:55:45,433 --> 00:55:47,100
- [Tom] You're living
in denial, Santa!

1472
00:55:47,100 --> 00:55:48,833
Wake up and smell the coffee!

1473
00:55:48,833 --> 00:55:50,667
- He's not like
Kimar and the others.

1474
00:55:50,667 --> 00:55:52,300
- I don't like him.

1475
00:55:52,300 --> 00:55:53,600
- I'm worried, Santa.

1476
00:55:53,600 --> 00:55:57,200
- Now, now, children,
let's not get excited.

1477
00:55:57,200 --> 00:55:58,300
- Help, help!

1478
00:55:59,500 --> 00:56:01,933
- [Joel] Now, what
would McGyver do?

1479
00:56:01,933 --> 00:56:04,300
- [Tom] This is great,
this is gonna be great!

1480
00:56:04,300 --> 00:56:05,567
Watch!

1481
00:56:05,567 --> 00:56:08,567
(suspenseful music)

1482
00:56:10,733 --> 00:56:11,967
- It's Voldar!

1483
00:56:11,967 --> 00:56:15,333
He's going to open
the space door!

1484
00:56:15,333 --> 00:56:16,533
Help, Kimar!

1485
00:56:16,533 --> 00:56:17,500
- Billy, please, now
you're embarrassing me.

1486
00:56:17,500 --> 00:56:19,233
- Kimar, help!

1487
00:56:19,233 --> 00:56:20,400
- [Joel] This is my time.

1488
00:56:20,400 --> 00:56:22,133
I feel good about me.

1489
00:56:25,433 --> 00:56:26,767
- [Tom] Come on!

1490
00:56:29,233 --> 00:56:30,800
I admire the plucky kid.

1491
00:56:30,800 --> 00:56:33,533
He really thinks on his
feet, a real booster.

1492
00:56:33,533 --> 00:56:34,367
- Stella!

1493
00:56:37,000 --> 00:56:38,600
- Gee, Santa, what
are we going to do?

1494
00:56:38,600 --> 00:56:41,467
Once the door opens, we
haven't got a chance.

1495
00:56:41,467 --> 00:56:46,067
- [Tom] We'll die a
horrible asphyxiated death.

1496
00:56:46,067 --> 00:56:48,700
- Where did you say
this leads to, Billy?

1497
00:56:48,700 --> 00:56:50,267
- Seven.
- Mississippi.

1498
00:56:50,267 --> 00:56:51,600
- Six.
- Mississippi.

1499
00:56:51,600 --> 00:56:53,300
- Five.
- Mississippi.

1500
00:56:53,300 --> 00:56:54,267
- [Tom] Connecticut.

1501
00:56:54,267 --> 00:56:55,100
- Four.
- Noonan.

1502
00:56:55,100 --> 00:56:56,100
- [Tom] Massachusetts.

1503
00:56:56,100 --> 00:56:57,167
- Three.
- Mississippi.

1504
00:56:57,167 --> 00:56:58,467
- Two.
- Feelin' good.

1505
00:56:58,467 --> 00:57:00,333
- One, zero.

1506
00:57:00,333 --> 00:57:01,367
- Ah, oh.

1507
00:57:01,367 --> 00:57:02,667
- Who's in the air lock?

1508
00:57:02,667 --> 00:57:04,367
- No one, now.

1509
00:57:04,367 --> 00:57:05,533
(gasping)

1510
00:57:05,533 --> 00:57:06,800
- What's going on, Voldar?

1511
00:57:06,800 --> 00:57:10,233
- Chief, Santa and the
children are missing!

1512
00:57:10,233 --> 00:57:11,733
- [Tom] I love you!

1513
00:57:11,733 --> 00:57:13,333
- It'll never work!

1514
00:57:14,567 --> 00:57:17,333
- Drifting around in space.

1515
00:57:17,333 --> 00:57:19,367
Along with the rest
of the space junk.

1516
00:57:19,367 --> 00:57:21,667
- My mother was junk,
don't talk like that!

1517
00:57:21,667 --> 00:57:23,700
- [Tom] (humming
dramatic music) Pow!

1518
00:57:23,700 --> 00:57:26,133
Boom, pow, zing, boof, choke!

1519
00:57:34,700 --> 00:57:38,400
- [Joel] Oh, he's fighting
the cameraman now.

1520
00:57:38,400 --> 00:57:40,833
- [Tom] Now we're in trouble.

1521
00:57:42,133 --> 00:57:43,533
- When I'm through
with you, Voldar,

1522
00:57:43,533 --> 00:57:45,967
you'll wish you were
floating out there in space!

1523
00:57:45,967 --> 00:57:47,300
(Santa laughing)

1524
00:57:47,300 --> 00:57:48,967
- Merry Christmas, everybody!

1525
00:57:48,967 --> 00:57:51,167
- Ah, Mr. Claus, you have
a nasty habit of surviving.

1526
00:57:51,167 --> 00:57:52,300
- Santa Claus, you're all right!

1527
00:57:52,300 --> 00:57:53,700
I thought you were--

1528
00:57:53,700 --> 00:57:57,100
- Well, when Voldar accidentally
left us in the airlock,

1529
00:57:57,100 --> 00:57:59,667
and then came up
here and accidentally

1530
00:57:59,667 --> 00:58:02,267
threw the door switch,
we knew we had to

1531
00:58:02,267 --> 00:58:04,233
get out of there
in a hurry, or that

1532
00:58:04,233 --> 00:58:07,200
would be the end of us.
- Uh, one, uh, two.

1533
00:58:07,200 --> 00:58:08,933
- Accidentally, of course.

1534
00:58:08,933 --> 00:58:10,700
- So we crawled out
through the air duct.

1535
00:58:10,700 --> 00:58:12,600
- The air duct?

1536
00:58:12,600 --> 00:58:14,133
- But the air duct
is just a little--

1537
00:58:14,133 --> 00:58:15,633
- Thing with the wheel and the--

1538
00:58:15,633 --> 00:58:17,967
(laughing)

1539
00:58:17,967 --> 00:58:19,300
- [Tom] Kill him.

1540
00:58:19,300 --> 00:58:21,667
- Why, you're talking
to Santa Claus, son.

1541
00:58:21,667 --> 00:58:23,633
(laughing)

1542
00:58:23,633 --> 00:58:24,867
- [Kimar] But how?

1543
00:58:24,867 --> 00:58:26,433
- Well, well now,
you wouldn't want me

1544
00:58:26,433 --> 00:58:28,833
to tell my secret, would you?

1545
00:58:31,300 --> 00:58:32,400
Oh, poor man.

1546
00:58:33,567 --> 00:58:35,667
- [Tom] He's bleeding
from the ears, too bad.

1547
00:58:35,667 --> 00:58:38,333
- He looks like someone
who's seen a ghost.

1548
00:58:38,333 --> 00:58:40,600
(laughing)

1549
00:58:44,167 --> 00:58:46,500
- Get my inhaler and my nitro!

1550
00:58:46,500 --> 00:58:49,167
- [Tom] Meanwhile, on the
Salyut 7 space station.

1551
00:58:49,167 --> 00:58:52,500
(dramatic music)

1552
00:58:52,500 --> 00:58:55,633
- [Joel] It's the Brunswick
bowling ball planet.

1553
00:58:55,633 --> 00:58:57,433
(Crow humming fanfare)

1554
00:58:57,433 --> 00:58:58,633
- [Kimar] Begin
landing operation.

1555
00:58:58,633 --> 00:59:01,367
- Firing retro rockets
one and two, fire.

1556
00:59:01,367 --> 00:59:02,500
(hissing)

1557
00:59:02,500 --> 00:59:04,100
- Lentils.
- Coulda guessed.

1558
00:59:04,100 --> 00:59:05,733
- Lower landing legs.

1559
00:59:05,733 --> 00:59:08,667
- [Tom] I said
don't call me legs.

1560
00:59:08,667 --> 00:59:10,633
- [Joel] Kevin, this is no
time to use the Nordic Track,

1561
00:59:10,633 --> 00:59:12,133
come on, man!

1562
00:59:12,133 --> 00:59:13,400
- Lower the ladder.

1563
00:59:13,400 --> 00:59:15,267
You and Hargo get
Voldar out of the brig

1564
00:59:15,267 --> 00:59:16,933
and take him to
the council room.

1565
00:59:16,933 --> 00:59:18,867
He'll stand trial immediately.

1566
00:59:18,867 --> 00:59:20,033
- All right, Chief.

1567
00:59:20,033 --> 00:59:21,700
- Don't call me Chief!

1568
00:59:21,700 --> 00:59:22,933
- We've landed.

1569
00:59:22,933 --> 00:59:23,833
- [Tom] You'll have to
take my word for it.

1570
00:59:23,833 --> 00:59:24,867
- Hatch open.

1571
00:59:24,867 --> 00:59:27,167
- Orrin Hatch.
- Hatch open.

1572
00:59:27,167 --> 00:59:28,500
- Ladder down.

1573
00:59:28,500 --> 00:59:29,433
- [Tom] Lauder?

1574
00:59:29,433 --> 00:59:31,400
- Power off, ship secure.

1575
00:59:33,000 --> 00:59:34,467
- [Tom] Nice Underoos.

1576
00:59:34,467 --> 00:59:37,167
♪ Jingle bells, jingle
bells, jingle all the way ♪

1577
00:59:37,167 --> 00:59:38,700
♪ Oh what fun it is to ride ♪

1578
00:59:38,700 --> 00:59:39,933
- [Joel] Oh, it's
a Tokyo apartment.

1579
00:59:39,933 --> 00:59:41,567
- No, it's the guy
from "Deliverance!"

1580
00:59:41,567 --> 00:59:43,133
♪ In a one-horse open sleigh ♪

1581
00:59:43,133 --> 00:59:44,500
- [Tom] Why are they
wearing Abdominizers?

1582
00:59:44,500 --> 00:59:45,900
- Merry Christmas, Voldar.

1583
00:59:45,900 --> 00:59:47,100
All right, on your
feet, come on.

1584
00:59:47,100 --> 00:59:49,833
(muffled shouting)

1585
00:59:49,833 --> 00:59:51,100
- Dropo!

1586
00:59:51,100 --> 00:59:53,500
- I was handing the food
pills through the bars,

1587
00:59:53,500 --> 00:59:55,167
and he grabbed my hand--
- Shut up!

1588
00:59:55,167 --> 00:59:56,333
- [Joel] Oh, you love it.

1589
00:59:56,333 --> 00:59:57,567
- Kimar!

1590
00:59:57,567 --> 00:59:59,300
- [Tom] When I call my
captain, I touch myself.

1591
00:59:59,300 --> 01:00:00,433
- Yes, Rigna.

1592
01:00:00,433 --> 01:00:01,900
- [Rigna] Voldar has escaped.

1593
01:00:01,900 --> 01:00:02,733
- What?

1594
01:00:02,733 --> 01:00:03,967
- He's gone.

1595
01:00:03,967 --> 01:00:05,400
- That can only mean trouble.

1596
01:00:05,400 --> 01:00:09,367
Put a constant guard on
Santa and the Earth children.

1597
01:00:09,367 --> 01:00:10,533
Voldar will be back.

1598
01:00:10,533 --> 01:00:12,667
- [Tom] In "Dial M for Martian."

1599
01:00:12,667 --> 01:00:14,833
(humming dramatic music)

1600
01:00:14,833 --> 01:00:18,600
- [Joel] I'll be out
in a minute, excuse me.

1601
01:00:18,600 --> 01:00:23,500
- [Tom] Previously, on "Santa
Claus Conquers the Martians."

1602
01:00:24,667 --> 01:00:28,400
- [Joel] Here in Betty
Crocker's test kitchen.

1603
01:00:29,433 --> 01:00:32,333
♪ I'll never smile ♪

1604
01:00:32,333 --> 01:00:33,267
- [Tom] Oh.

1605
01:00:33,267 --> 01:00:34,733
- Mother, is Father here yet?

1606
01:00:34,733 --> 01:00:36,800
- No, Bomar, I'll call
you the moment he arrives.

1607
01:00:36,800 --> 01:00:39,067
- Is Dropo coming back too?

1608
01:00:39,067 --> 01:00:41,967
- Yes, Girmar, now go
back to your studies.

1609
01:00:41,967 --> 01:00:44,633
- [Joel] Go play with
your Golden Globe award.

1610
01:00:44,633 --> 01:00:47,167
- [Tom] That we bought for you.

1611
01:00:51,133 --> 01:00:54,233
(all humming "Dick
Van Dyke Show" theme)

1612
01:00:54,233 --> 01:00:55,333
- [Joel] Sh, not now.

1613
01:00:55,333 --> 01:00:56,300
- Oh, Kimar!

1614
01:00:56,300 --> 01:00:57,633
- Kimar is the savings place.

1615
01:00:57,633 --> 01:00:59,667
- [Tom] Headbutt.

1616
01:00:59,667 --> 01:01:00,833
- Are you alone?

1617
01:01:00,833 --> 01:01:01,667
- No.

1618
01:01:04,800 --> 01:01:05,967
- [Momar] Well!

1619
01:01:05,967 --> 01:01:07,900
- [Kimar] Earthlings,
Billy and Betty.

1620
01:01:07,900 --> 01:01:09,967
- One of each flavor.

1621
01:01:09,967 --> 01:01:12,600
- Welcome to our home.

1622
01:01:12,600 --> 01:01:14,033
- [All] Headbutt.

1623
01:01:14,933 --> 01:01:15,900
Headbutt.

1624
01:01:15,900 --> 01:01:17,933
- There's someone else, too.

1625
01:01:17,933 --> 01:01:19,600
Come on, come on in!

1626
01:01:19,600 --> 01:01:20,467
- [Tom] You may have
to grease the door

1627
01:01:20,467 --> 01:01:21,733
for him to get through.

1628
01:01:21,733 --> 01:01:24,400
(chuckling) A big ol' haul.

1629
01:01:24,400 --> 01:01:25,367
- Ho ho ho!

1630
01:01:25,367 --> 01:01:26,600
Lady Momar.

1631
01:01:26,600 --> 01:01:29,100
I'm not accustomed to
entering people's homes

1632
01:01:29,100 --> 01:01:32,533
through the door, but
you have no chimney.

1633
01:01:32,533 --> 01:01:34,600
- [Joel] Breaking and
entering, that's my racket.

1634
01:01:34,600 --> 01:01:36,133
- Welcome, Santa
Claus, we hope you'll

1635
01:01:36,133 --> 01:01:38,367
make the children
on Mars very happy.

1636
01:01:38,367 --> 01:01:39,800
- I'll try, dear lady.

1637
01:01:39,800 --> 01:01:40,967
(Tom imitating kissing)

1638
01:01:40,967 --> 01:01:42,300
- But I get a per diem.

1639
01:01:42,300 --> 01:01:44,900
(mellow music)

1640
01:01:48,767 --> 01:01:50,200
- Where are they?

1641
01:01:50,200 --> 01:01:52,267
- Well, we'll start
with my youngsters.

1642
01:01:52,267 --> 01:01:53,833
How are they, Momar?

1643
01:01:53,833 --> 01:01:54,800
- The same.

1644
01:01:54,800 --> 01:01:57,033
Quiet, remote, and very unhappy.

1645
01:01:57,033 --> 01:01:58,267
They're inside studying.

1646
01:01:58,267 --> 01:01:59,533
- [Tom] They've been
reading "The Bell Jar."

1647
01:01:59,533 --> 01:02:01,567
- Let old Santa
say hello to them.

1648
01:02:01,567 --> 01:02:04,567
And I'm sure these children
would like to meet them.

1649
01:02:04,567 --> 01:02:07,000
- I'll tell them you're here.

1650
01:02:08,033 --> 01:02:09,567
- [Computer] Y over five.

1651
01:02:09,567 --> 01:02:11,467
- [Tom] Tony Danza
is a fine actor.

1652
01:02:11,467 --> 01:02:13,100
Sinbad is funny.

1653
01:02:13,100 --> 01:02:15,633
Blake Edwards makes
a really good film.

1654
01:02:15,633 --> 01:02:18,167
- [Computer] Traveling
along vector A.

1655
01:02:18,167 --> 01:02:21,633
- [Joel] You are
powerful, you can sell.

1656
01:02:21,633 --> 01:02:23,433
- [Computer] And the
power of 12 megatrons.

1657
01:02:23,433 --> 01:02:25,667
- Father, Father, we missed you!

1658
01:02:25,667 --> 01:02:28,433
- Ha ha, I missed you too.

1659
01:02:28,433 --> 01:02:31,433
- [Tom] I'm fine, Dmitri,
you're fine, we're both fine.

1660
01:02:31,433 --> 01:02:33,267
It's good to be fine.
- I've brought some visitors.

1661
01:02:33,267 --> 01:02:34,167
From Earth.

1662
01:02:35,767 --> 01:02:37,200
Will you come in
please, children?

1663
01:02:37,200 --> 01:02:40,233
- [Joel] And sign in, please.

1664
01:02:40,233 --> 01:02:43,900
- Billy and Betty, this
is Bomar and Girmar.

1665
01:02:45,567 --> 01:02:46,400
- Hi.

1666
01:02:48,333 --> 01:02:50,733
- [Joel] Wait, where's
that thing been?

1667
01:02:50,733 --> 01:02:52,100
- There's nothing in it.

1668
01:02:52,100 --> 01:02:53,667
What are you giving me?

1669
01:02:53,667 --> 01:02:55,300
- My hand, to shake.

1670
01:02:58,000 --> 01:03:01,633
- [Tom] (buzzing)
Oh, I love that gag.

1671
01:03:01,633 --> 01:03:03,733
- [Joel] It's getting
uncomfortable now.

1672
01:03:03,733 --> 01:03:05,400
- How old are you?
- I'm 10.

1673
01:03:05,400 --> 01:03:08,033
- I'm 10 too, and
Girmar's eight.

1674
01:03:08,033 --> 01:03:09,200
- So's my sister.

1675
01:03:09,200 --> 01:03:10,400
- [Tom] So's your
sister, and your mother

1676
01:03:10,400 --> 01:03:11,900
swims out to troop ships.

1677
01:03:11,900 --> 01:03:13,500
- There's another Earth
person that wants to see you.

1678
01:03:13,500 --> 01:03:14,767
- [Joel] His name
is B.F. Skinner.

1679
01:03:14,767 --> 01:03:18,333
He's going to put
you kids in a box.

1680
01:03:18,333 --> 01:03:20,667
(chuckling)

1681
01:03:24,000 --> 01:03:26,967
- Dad, get him outta here!

1682
01:03:26,967 --> 01:03:29,033
- [Tom] Santa left his
medication at home.

1683
01:03:29,033 --> 01:03:32,333
- [Joel] (laughing) Dad, Dad!

1684
01:03:32,333 --> 01:03:36,633
(all laughing hysterically)

1685
01:03:36,633 --> 01:03:38,967
(screaming)

1686
01:03:48,767 --> 01:03:50,033
What is that, an outtake from

1687
01:03:50,033 --> 01:03:52,133
"TV's Bloopers and
Practical Jokes?"

1688
01:03:52,133 --> 01:03:53,367
- You know, it's
the little things

1689
01:03:53,367 --> 01:03:54,433
that can clue you
into drug abuse.

1690
01:03:54,433 --> 01:03:55,567
- They're laughing.

1691
01:03:55,567 --> 01:03:57,000
Bomar and Girmar, too.

1692
01:03:57,000 --> 01:04:00,067
- They've never laughed before.

1693
01:04:00,067 --> 01:04:01,600
- Come.

1694
01:04:01,600 --> 01:04:02,867
- [Tom] Come on, let's go
catch the end of his act.

1695
01:04:02,867 --> 01:04:05,233
He does this killer
drive-up window gag.

1696
01:04:05,233 --> 01:04:08,267
(playful music)

1697
01:04:08,267 --> 01:04:10,533
- [Joel] He'll be
the first to die.

1698
01:04:10,533 --> 01:04:11,533
- Ah, a cave dweller!

1699
01:04:11,533 --> 01:04:12,800
No?

1700
01:04:12,800 --> 01:04:14,767
- Me, Voldar, hiding
in a dirty cave

1701
01:04:14,767 --> 01:04:17,000
like a speckled Mars worm.

1702
01:04:17,000 --> 01:04:20,100
Oh, Kimar will get
this, I'll find a way.

1703
01:04:20,100 --> 01:04:21,633
- That's easy.

1704
01:04:21,633 --> 01:04:23,933
Let's get rid of his little
fat friend in the red suit.

1705
01:04:23,933 --> 01:04:25,733
- [Joel] Taffy apple, boss?

1706
01:04:25,733 --> 01:04:26,567
Ahh.

1707
01:04:26,567 --> 01:04:27,900
- That's suicide.

1708
01:04:27,900 --> 01:04:29,300
- [Tom] What do you
mean, whack Santa?

1709
01:04:29,300 --> 01:04:31,233
What are you, nuts?
- He's under constant guard.

1710
01:04:31,233 --> 01:04:33,000
We couldn't get within 20
feet of him without being--

1711
01:04:33,000 --> 01:04:34,967
- [Joel] What is this, a
soliloquy all of a sudden, whoa!

1712
01:04:34,967 --> 01:04:36,533
- I have other plans.

1713
01:04:36,533 --> 01:04:37,567
(dramatic music)

1714
01:04:37,567 --> 01:04:39,300
- Who's playing that?

1715
01:04:40,767 --> 01:04:42,233
- Someone's
approaching the cave!

1716
01:04:42,233 --> 01:04:43,533
- [Tom] The king approaches!

1717
01:04:43,533 --> 01:04:45,067
- It's me, Shim!

1718
01:04:45,067 --> 01:04:46,833
- All right.
- Jim?

1719
01:04:46,833 --> 01:04:49,267
- [Joel] It's Big Jim McLain.

1720
01:04:51,167 --> 01:04:53,200
- All right, Shim, enter.

1721
01:04:53,200 --> 01:04:56,867
- Enter, what
happened to come in?

1722
01:04:56,867 --> 01:04:58,133
- What did you find out?

1723
01:04:58,133 --> 01:05:00,200
- The toy shop is
operating full blast.

1724
01:05:00,200 --> 01:05:01,967
No one suspects me.
- Ha-cha!

1725
01:05:01,967 --> 01:05:03,867
- So I sneaked down and
took a good long look.

1726
01:05:03,867 --> 01:05:05,333
It's nothing like
the one on Earth.

1727
01:05:05,333 --> 01:05:07,433
- [Tom] Goodnight, Mrs.
Calabash, wherever you are.

